WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:10.720
- So I'm John Geanakoplos,

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:14.103
the chair of Hellenic studies department,

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:16.920
and a professor in economics,

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.990
and I'd like to welcome you all here.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.079
I'm so glad to see so many of you,

00:00:21.079 --> 00:00:25.050
so glad to see a previous
chair, Staffis Khalivas,

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.581
back from Oxford, here to
join us for these talks.

00:00:28.581 --> 00:00:32.310
These lectures bring to Yale every year,

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:34.930
this is the 15th one of them,

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:38.005
distinguished scholars in the humanities,

00:00:38.005 --> 00:00:41.940
or the social sciences,
or a public figure,

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.140
or an artist, or somebody of
an international reputation.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.023
Yannis is all of those.

00:00:49.085 --> 00:00:52.870
And as you probably know, the
Stavros Niarchos Foundation

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:55.899
has been the primary
sponsor of these lectures

00:00:55.899 --> 00:01:00.090
since the program had its beginnings.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:03.250
In fact, the Niarchos Foundation founded

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:07.110
the Hellenic Studies program,
as a pilot program, in 2001.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:12.110
And then in 2007, it established
it as a permanent program.

00:01:12.336 --> 00:01:15.482
And the Niarchos Foundation has therefore

00:01:15.482 --> 00:01:18.000
created Hellenic Studies in Yale,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.710
but that's not all it does.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:24.710
It's worked all over the
campus to provide activities

00:01:24.897 --> 00:01:28.620
in the School of Art, the Peabody Museum,

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.860
the Center for
Globalization, all over Yale.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:37.060
But not just all over
Yale, all over the country.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:40.120
So this is the Niarchos Foundation

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.640
that opened up recently in Athens,

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:46.171
spectacular building that
you've probably been to.

00:01:46.171 --> 00:01:50.643
This is, in the center here, is the,

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:55.643
well that's the outgoing President
of the Yale Undergraduate

00:01:56.270 --> 00:02:00.070
Greek Students Association, Daphne Martin.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:02.480
And she's there with three of her friends,

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.550
the four of them from Yale,

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:09.550
went to Sparta to help
sponsor the rebuilding

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:11.570
of the archeological museum,

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:16.530
and to give tours of the
current archeological museum.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.240
And I happened to be there at the time

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.840
and I read about them in the newspaper

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.690
and I rushed over to get a tour.

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.267
It was quite wonderful.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:26.080
And I brought along my cousin, Anser,

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.357
whom you see on the side here.

00:02:28.357 --> 00:02:29.680
(laughing)

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.550
Who turned out to be a rap singer

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:37.870
and possibly the second most
famous rap singer in Greece.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:40.770
But anyway, he's also
a charging accomplice.

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:41.940
So what happened?

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.620
While I was there, of course,
I visited all my relatives,

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.170
in a little town called Theologos,

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:48.446
and here are some of them.

00:02:48.446 --> 00:02:50.178
There are more of them.

00:02:50.178 --> 00:02:53.140
So the Niarchos Foundation, turns out,

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:56.730
does a lot in Athens, in Sparta,

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:59.584
because Niarchos himself comes from a town

00:02:59.584 --> 00:03:02.516
in Laconia called Vamvakou.

00:03:02.516 --> 00:03:05.550
And so, for example,
the Niarchos Foundation

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.400
is building a hospital in Sparta,

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.750
designed by Renzo Piano.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:15.490
And, most interesting to
me, the foundation decided

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:18.030
that there are not
enough young people left

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.348
in these beautiful villages.

00:03:20.348 --> 00:03:23.250
The people are aging and the young people

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:24.930
are moving out of the villages,

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:29.890
and they're paying them
now for grade schoolers

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:34.180
from Athens to visit
Vamvakou during the summer

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.550
and see what it's like,

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:37.610
see what the culture of
the villages were like.

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:41.050
And also bring a little life
and energy to the villages.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:44.510
Here is Vamvakou, you see what
a beautiful village it is.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:48.850
And the long term
residents are under 20 now.

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:51.670
I mean, a disappearing village.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:54.520
So of course Vamvakou
is not the only village

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:56.650
in the hills above Sparta,

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:00.210
where the people left
are a little bit old.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:05.210
You can imagine Theologos being
part of the program shortly.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:08.110
Well it turns out that Vamvakou

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:12.603
was only 30 kilometers from Theologos,

00:04:12.603 --> 00:04:15.600
and I'm related to the Niarchos,

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.273
as I found out this summer.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:21.173
So, Anser, who you saw before,

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.940
my grandfather's nephew
was Anser's grandfather,

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:29.660
married Anser's grandmother,
the Sarantopoulos family,

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:33.229
who was a second cousin
to Stavros Niarchos.

00:04:33.229 --> 00:04:34.580
You know, the more I talk to my family,

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.260
I realize we're related to the Niarchos,

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:37.650
I didn't realize that.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.400
Actually, my family might
have been doing better

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.209
than the Niarchos center.

00:04:41.209 --> 00:04:44.420
So it turns out that my grandfather,

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:47.102
my grandmother, was the richest girl

00:04:47.102 --> 00:04:50.050
and this is the house she grew up in

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:55.000
in the late 1800s, she was
born in the late 1800s.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:58.520
It's now military center of Sparta.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.220
But if you've been to Sparta,

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.325
you'll know there are not
many houses like that.

00:05:02.325 --> 00:05:03.920
That's where my grandmother
would have lived.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:08.190
So, my grandfather left
Theologos at the age of 12

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:11.940
in 1892, by himself, and came to America,

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:13.420
and built a candy factory.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:16.890
And this is the candy
factory on Lake Hennepin

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:19.790
in Minneapolis, the first
Greek in Minneapolis.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.090
You can see the Geanakoplos name.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:25.020
There it is blown up a little
bit, the Geanakoplos name.

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:30.020
And, thank you, recently,
it's been remodeled.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:32.223
(laughing)

00:05:32.223 --> 00:05:35.111
It's now part of Calhoun Square

00:05:35.111 --> 00:05:40.111
and the singer for
Minneapolis, known as Prince,

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:43.970
wrote a song about Calhoun Square,

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:45.470
my grandfather's candy factory.

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:47.765
So, I ask you, no.

00:05:47.765 --> 00:05:50.015
(laughing)

00:05:53.413 --> 00:05:57.996
So, today, we're very lucky
that the article's lecturer

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.140
is Yannis Stournaras.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:04.730
He is a man, as I said at the
beginning, who's done it all.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:08.400
He combines all the desirable qualities

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.920
of the article speaker.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:11.850
He's an undergraduate at
the University of Athens.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:15.700
He got his Masters at
Oxford, his PhD at Oxford,

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:18.304
in Economic Theory and Policy.

00:06:18.304 --> 00:06:20.900
He became a Lecturer and Research fellow

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:22.700
at St. Catherine's College in Oxford.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:25.900
Then he came back to Green
and was a Special Advisor

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:29.140
to the Ministry of Finance
at the Bank of Greece,

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:32.430
a Professor at the
University of Athens in 1989.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:34.850
I decided I wanted a little
more detail about this.

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:39.530
So, one of my partners in a
business I run on the side,

00:06:39.530 --> 00:06:44.300
his sister, Vicky Nicopoulos,
went to grade school

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:48.080
with Yannis and she said,

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.510
he was quick witted and very smart,

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:53.114
at least between the ages of 11 and 14,

00:06:53.114 --> 00:06:56.010
when we took a tutorial
together in English.

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:59.321
And he had curly, reddish-blonde hair.

00:06:59.321 --> 00:07:01.450
(laughing)

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:05.020
So, but Yannis after than became Chairman

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:08.360
of the Council of Economic
Advisers from 1994 to 2000,

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:12.340
in a crucial time for Greece
when they joined the EU.

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:15.913
So, just before the
European Monetary Union,

00:07:16.968 --> 00:07:21.430
he became President and
CEO of Emporiki Bank,

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:24.318
the Vice Chair of the
Association of Greek Banks,

00:07:24.318 --> 00:07:28.960
the Minister of Finance in 2012 to 2014

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.720
and the Governor of the Bank of Greece.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.900
Now, not only does he do all these things,

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:35.790
he's also a mesmerizing speaker.

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:38.740
When I was there in 2013,

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:43.740
I was in So-union and there
was a talk in the moonlight

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:48.620
at the Temple of Poseidon that Yannis gave

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:52.570
and I was trying to remember
if the mythological theme

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:54.780
that he carried throughout
this whole talk.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.988
I'm afraid I have forgotten it though.

00:07:56.988 --> 00:07:57.821
But it was a beautiful speech.

00:07:57.821 --> 00:08:01.490
So, let me say, again, how glad I am

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:04.630
to welcome all of you here
to meet article lecturers

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:09.170
and especially how glad I am
to welcome Yannis Stournaras,

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:11.810
even though this isn't quite
the Temple of Poseidon,

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:14.635
it's the Yale University, welcome Yannis.

00:08:14.635 --> 00:08:16.885
(applause)

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:28.750
- Thank you, thank you, John.
I think, if I remember well,

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:33.440
I must have told you an
anecdote about Delphi

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:42.440
if I remember well, it
was because at that time,

00:08:43.104 --> 00:08:46.800
at that time, there was a
controversy at which university

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.880
was better, Oxford or Cambridge?

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.000
So, the legation of both universities,

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:54.063
they went to Delphi to ask the Oracle.

00:08:55.210 --> 00:08:56.970
So they asked the Oracle.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.789
The Oracle using all the usual stuff.

00:08:59.789 --> 00:09:02.157
She took hours and hours.

00:09:02.157 --> 00:09:05.820
And then, at the end she turned them

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:07.567
and said, "What is Cambridge?"

00:09:07.567 --> 00:09:09.817
(laughing)

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:18.970
Well, it's a really great
honor for me to be invited

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:23.280
to deliver the annual Stavros
Niarchos Foundation lecture.

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:24.730
The Hellenic Studies Program

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:27.760
at the Yale Macmillan Center
does an excellent job.

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:29.260
I had the opportunity to visit

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:34.260
some of the rooms here and
some of the colleagues.

00:09:34.343 --> 00:09:35.960
In studying and promoting

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:38.810
contemporary Greek culture and history.

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:41.200
So in my talk today, I will first present

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:43.680
the lessons to be drawn
from the Greek crisis.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.450
By the way, the title of this speech

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:49.380
will be "Greece in Europe:
The Reasons for Optimism".

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:52.390
So I will then discuss the
progress made in recent years

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:54.456
and the outlook for the Greek economy,

00:09:54.456 --> 00:09:57.090
and highlight the crisis legacies

00:09:57.090 --> 00:09:59.120
and the challenges that lie ahead,

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:01.710
both for Greece and Euro zone.

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:04.790
Finally, I will put forward
some policy proposals

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:06.530
for addressing these challenges,

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:09.113
both for Greece and the Euro area.

00:10:10.163 --> 00:10:13.750
From 2000 to 2007, Greece experienced

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.560
benign macroeconommic conditions

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:18.650
characterized by high rates of GDP growth,

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:21.720
well above the Euro area average,

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.180
relatively stable
consumer price inflation,

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.581
and a gradually decreasing
unemployment rate.

00:10:26.581 --> 00:10:30.000
The expanision was driven
mainly by rapid credit growth

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.117
and low borrowing costs following
financial liberalization

00:10:33.117 --> 00:10:37.269
and Greece's entry into EMU in 2001.

00:10:37.269 --> 00:10:41.310
The mastrate criteria for joining

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:43.400
Economic and Monetary Union were

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:47.800
based solely on nominal
conversions and therefore,

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:50.657
failed to incentivize
the structural reforms

00:10:50.657 --> 00:10:52.963
in the product and labor markets.

00:10:53.801 --> 00:10:55.230
And the functioning of the public sector

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:58.270
needed to enhance real conversions,

00:10:58.270 --> 00:11:00.820
raise potential growth, and safe guard

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:03.370
the system ability of public finances.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:05.700
On the contrary, employer and employee,

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:07.700
there as groups, opposed the reforms

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:09.800
that would have increased competitiveness.

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:13.610
Also, Greece's GDP per capita increased

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:15.612
during the boom period approaching

00:11:15.612 --> 00:11:18.410
the European Union average.

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:20.130
The institutional GAP relatively

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:21.833
to the Euro area did not narrow.

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:24.910
Thus Greece continued to lag significantly

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:29.190
behind its Euro area partners
in various indicators

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:31.523
of governance and
structural competitiveness.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:34.550
The sub deterioration of the fiscal

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:38.564
and macroeconomic
environment in 2008 and 2009

00:11:38.564 --> 00:11:41.250
and the subsequent
downgrades of sovereign debt

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:45.240
and rising sovereign spreads
cut off the Greek sovereign

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:48.390
and banks from international
capital and money markets.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.340
Substantial deposit withdrawals

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:52.790
and extremely tied legal conditions

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:57.730
put strain on the
banking sector and EUIMF,

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:01.960
Finance Economic Adjustment
Program, was initiated in 2010,

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:04.700
aiming to correct these imbalances.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.270
The crisis has taken a heavy toll

00:12:07.270 --> 00:12:09.880
on output, incomes, and the world.

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:14.760
Between 2008 and 2016,
Greece lost over one-fourth

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:17.920
of it's GDP at constant prices
and the unemployment rate

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:21.037
rose by nearly 16 percentage points.

00:12:21.037 --> 00:12:24.450
Furthermore, GDP per
capita and purchasing power

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:29.450
of parity declined to 67.4%
of the EU average in 2018,

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:36.710
down from 93.3% in 2008.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:41.520
To this, one must add the large increase

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:44.390
of non performing loans,
that is the NPL ratio

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:46.640
to about 50% of the total.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:50.150
The large brain drain and
massive underinvestment

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:54.080
with an immeasurable economic
and social consequences.

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:57.660
The slide of the GDP growth
rate into negative territory

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:01.230
raised the debt to GDP ratio
to unsustainable levels,

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:04.030
despite the fiscal
consolidation and caused

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:07.533
their servicing problems for
high schools and businesses.

00:13:07.533 --> 00:13:10.550
This was the main but
not the exclusive reason

00:13:10.550 --> 00:13:13.920
why non performing
loans rose dramatically,

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:16.060
weakening bank's acid quality,

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:19.063
thus making difficult for banks
to finance the real economy.

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:22.520
It took no less than eight years,

00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:24.410
three economic adjustment programs,

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:26.590
major debt restructuring, and three rounds

00:13:26.590 --> 00:13:30.923
of bank recapitalization to
resolve the Greek crisis.

00:13:32.190 --> 00:13:34.770
The length and depth of the Greek crisis

00:13:34.770 --> 00:13:37.260
can be explained by seven factors.

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:39.980
First, the size and speed

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:42.373
of fiscal consolidation
were unprecedented.

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:45.660
This is primarily hard to do with the fact

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:49.340
that the initial fiscal
and accelerating balances

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:51.650
were much higher in Greece than

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:55.270
in other member states
on the financial stretch.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:58.440
In addition, emphasis has,
on average, been placed

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:01.690
over the three adjustment
programs, more on tax hikes,

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:03.630
rather than on expenditure cuts,

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:07.230
growth and housing reforms,
and privatizations.

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:10.560
Second, the fiscal
multipliers turned out to be

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:12.730
higher than initially anticipated.

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:14.130
And the economy was soon caught

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:17.420
in a viscous circle of
hostility and recession.

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:20.700
Third, the second state
of structural reforms

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:22.560
led to real wages declining

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:27.310
more than initially expected,
exacerbating the recession.

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:29.870
In other words, the reform effort focused

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:31.343
much more on the labor market

00:14:31.343 --> 00:14:33.650
than on the goods and services markets.

00:14:33.650 --> 00:14:36.570
Hence, nominal wages declined faster

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:38.640
and more strongly than prices.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:40.670
Households experienced a massive drop

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:42.860
in purchasing power, which in turn,

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:45.883
constrained personal consumption
and deepened the recession.

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:50.070
Fourth, the non performing loans problem

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:52.000
proved very difficult to manage.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:54.400
Mainly the result of economic contraction,

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:57.720
it as further exacerbated
by legislative changes,

00:14:57.720 --> 00:14:59.400
such as the blanket mediatorial

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:00.827
on primary residence auctions

00:15:00.827 --> 00:15:03.780
and the abuse of foreclosure protection,

00:15:03.780 --> 00:15:07.580
as well as several other legal
and judicial impediments.

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:09.105
With the benefit of hindsight,

00:15:09.105 --> 00:15:11.900
it could be said that
a more dynamic response

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:14.140
during the first years of the crisis,

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:17.400
implementing the necessary
legislative change much earlier,

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:21.050
and introducing a systemic
solution by a centralized,

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:24.012
acid ]] for non performing
loans as other members

00:15:24.012 --> 00:15:27.913
said hadam, could have reduced
the problem we face today.

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:32.340
Fifth, certain reforms fell behind

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:35.950
their Greek time schedule on
account of a number of factors,

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:40.600
including insufficient ownership
of the necessary reforms,

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:43.570
population rhetoric, political rivalry,

00:15:43.570 --> 00:15:47.410
and the resistance of various
vested interests to reform.

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:49.650
This had serious consequences.

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:52.540
The signing of a third
economic adjustment program,

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:55.020
the introduction of
capital controls mainly

00:15:56.159 --> 00:15:57.422
to stem the outflow of bank deposits,

00:15:57.422 --> 00:16:00.090
and other bank recapitalization rounds.

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:02.760
In two years of economic stagnation.

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:04.900
Sixth, political deliberations

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:07.300
in the Euro area also played their part

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:09.820
in delaying the recovery
of the Greek economy.

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:13.320
The Euro group decision of November 2012

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:16.160
to grant further debt relief was put off

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:19.923
for a number of years and was
only implemented in June 2018.

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:24.350
This undermines the growth prospects

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:27.006
of the Greek economy and
prolonged the crashes.

00:16:27.006 --> 00:16:29.720
Had this form of debt relief been given

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:32.460
at the beginning of the first
economic adjustment program,

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:36.100
alongside the implementation
of ambitious growth

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:37.263
and housing structural reform

00:16:37.263 --> 00:16:39.390
and the national management company

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:41.820
to deal with the problem
of non performing loans,

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:44.930
it would have had a more
positive impact on the economy,

00:16:44.930 --> 00:16:48.830
possibly limiting output
and employment losses.

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:52.197
Seventh, when the Greek crisis broke out.

00:16:52.197 --> 00:16:54.530
The Economic and Monetary Union lacked

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:58.160
the tools to prevent
or contain the crisis.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:00.700
The stability and growth
part failed to control

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:04.068
the buildup of public debt
in the big crisis period.

00:17:04.068 --> 00:17:06.120
There was insufficient monetary

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:08.319
and control over macroeconomic
imbalances such as

00:17:08.319 --> 00:17:12.840
the evolution of the current
account and private debt.

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:15.540
The sovereign bank, Dumloop,

00:17:15.540 --> 00:17:18.780
amplified the financial
crisis in the recession.

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:21.447
Euro area crisis management
and the resolution tools

00:17:21.447 --> 00:17:24.810
were poor or even nonexistent on account

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:28.720
of highly exaggerated
concerns about moral hazard.

00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:31.890
And due to the lack of an
appropriate institutional setting,

00:17:31.890 --> 00:17:34.070
there was no provisional for risk sharing

00:17:35.307 --> 00:17:36.810
in the initial EMU architecture.

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:41.400
It was this business response,
especially after mid-2012,

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:45.300
which provided the time required
for Euro area governments

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:47.872
to take the actions necessary to safegaurd

00:17:47.872 --> 00:17:50.270
the stability of the financial system

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:52.420
and strengthen Economic
and Monetary Union.

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:58.720
Despite the missteps, the
occasional backsliding and delays,

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:00.840
significant progress has been made

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:04.760
since the beginning of the
sovereign debt crisis in 2010.

00:18:04.760 --> 00:18:07.340
The implementation of
economic adjustment programs

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:10.370
has eliminated the root
causes of the Greek crisis.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:13.300
More specifically, the
achieved fiscal adjustment

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:16.370
was unprecedented,
turning a primary deficit

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:20.320
of 10% of GDP in 2009
into a primary surplus

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:23.837
of 4.3% of GDP in 2018.

00:18:23.837 --> 00:18:27.230
The primary surplus in 2018 exceeded

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:29.873
the program target for
the fourth year in a row.

00:18:30.990 --> 00:18:32.890
The current account
deficit has been reduced

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:34.810
by 12 percentage points of GDP

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:37.470
since the beginning of the crisis.

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:39.500
Labor cost competitiveness has been

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:41.800
fully restored and price competitiveness

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:45.083
has recorded substantial gains since 2009.

00:18:46.159 --> 00:18:49.715
A bold program of structural
reforms was implemented,

00:18:49.715 --> 00:18:51.950
covering such areas as the pension

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:55.110
and healthcare systems,
goods and services markets,

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:57.420
the business environment, the tax system,

00:18:57.420 --> 00:19:00.630
the budgeted reform work, and
public sector transparency.

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:03.400
The banking system has been restructured.

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:05.930
Today, only four systemic banks control

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:10.870
over 95% of the market, as
more than 10 other banks

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:13.230
were merged or liquidated.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:15.090
The role of the Bank of Greece was pivotal

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:17.320
in the restructuring and recapitalization

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:19.250
of the banking system, the enhancement

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:20.640
of it's corporate governance,

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:23.460
and the provision of
liquidity all over Greece,

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:26.078
especially during the crisis years.

00:19:26.078 --> 00:19:29.140
Today, bank's capital adequacy ratio stand

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:32.710
at rather satisfactory levels
and their long loss provisions

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:35.769
are sufficient to address
potential credit risks.

00:19:35.769 --> 00:19:39.436
A number of important reforms
have been implemented,

00:19:39.436 --> 00:19:41.890
aiming to provide the banks with an array

00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:44.920
of tools for tackling the
problem of non performing loans,

00:19:44.920 --> 00:19:48.600
including the strengthening
of the supervisory framework

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:50.310
by setting operational targets

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:53.270
for non performing loan reduction,

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:56.650
the creation of a secondary
non performing loan market,

00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:58.190
and the removal of various legal,

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:00.660
judicial, and a new set of barriers

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:03.590
through the management
of non performing loans.

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:06.121
This action has started to bear fruit,

00:20:06.121 --> 00:20:09.860
as shown by the continuous reduction

00:20:09.860 --> 00:20:11.916
of the non performing loans stock

00:20:11.916 --> 00:20:14.120
in line with the targets set.

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:18.720
Non performing loans amounted
to 75.4 billion Euros

00:20:18.720 --> 00:20:23.510
at the end of June 2019
down by almost 32 billion

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:26.450
from the peak in March 2016.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:31.450
However, the impel ratio remains
high at 43.6% in June 2019.

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:36.420
As a result of the reforms implemented

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:38.310
since the beginning of the crisis

00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:41.170
and the effort of enterprises to make up

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:44.840
for declining domestic demand
by exporting to new markets,

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:47.050
openness has increased substantially

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:48.820
and the economy has started to rebalance

00:20:48.820 --> 00:20:52.170
over trade double export-oriented sectors.

00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:54.660
The sear of total exports in GDP increased

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:59.660
from 19% in 2009, to 36% in 2018.

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:01.490
Exports of goods and services,

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:03.340
excluding the sleeping sector,

00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:08.270
have increased in real terms
by 60% since the draft in 2009,

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:11.310
outperforming Euro area
exports as a whole.

00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:13.940
The volume of trade
double goods and services

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:16.250
in the economy increased cumulatively

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:21.250
between 2010 and 2017
by approximately 14%,

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:24.410
relative to non trade doubles
in terms of gross value added.

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:30.020
Following the stagnation of 2015 and 2016,

00:21:30.020 --> 00:21:32.853
GDP growth returned to
positive territory in 2017,

00:21:34.052 --> 00:21:38.370
for it grew by 1.5% and
peaked up to 1.9% in 2018.

00:21:40.490 --> 00:21:43.900
Recent real GDP data pointed
to continue expansion in

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:48.900
the second quarter of 2019,
which about 1.9% year on year.

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:53.983
Thanks to the improved economic conditions

00:21:53.983 --> 00:21:57.140
and the reforms implemented since 2010,

00:21:57.140 --> 00:21:59.700
the unemployment rate, though still high,

00:21:59.700 --> 00:22:04.660
fell the 16.9% in the
second quarter of 2019,

00:22:04.660 --> 00:22:08.363
from 27.8% at the end of 2017.

00:22:09.243 --> 00:22:11.810
Moving forward, the Bank of Greece expects

00:22:11.810 --> 00:22:14.470
that economic activity will remain

00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:16.890
on a positive growth trajectory,

00:22:16.890 --> 00:22:21.890
expanding by 1.9% for
the whole year of 2019,

00:22:22.210 --> 00:22:25.250
that is by 2.3% year on year

00:22:25.250 --> 00:22:27.930
in the second semester
of the current year.

00:22:27.930 --> 00:22:31.723
And double of 2% next year, in 2020.

00:22:32.940 --> 00:22:36.150
The outlook is, of course,
subject to downside risks

00:22:36.150 --> 00:22:37.920
related both to the external,

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:40.290
but also the domestic environment.

00:22:40.290 --> 00:22:42.740
The global growth and trade slow down

00:22:42.740 --> 00:22:46.140
due to imminent trade war
could affect export growth

00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:48.885
more markedly, while the disorderly Brexit

00:22:48.885 --> 00:22:51.778
drew political tensions and
the recent increasing prices

00:22:51.778 --> 00:22:55.290
are further significant downside risks.

00:22:55.290 --> 00:22:57.387
A possible set of corrections
in a global capital

00:22:57.387 --> 00:23:00.379
and financial market
could increase the cost

00:23:00.379 --> 00:23:01.720
and reduce the availability of funding,

00:23:01.720 --> 00:23:04.200
particularly for the private sector.

00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:07.240
There are also downside
risks on the fiscal front,

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:11.510
associated with ongoing
cultural leaks, on pension cuts,

00:23:11.510 --> 00:23:13.683
which could weigh on their sustainability.

00:23:15.250 --> 00:23:17.080
In addition, an exacerbation

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:19.653
of the refugee crisis could scare tourism.

00:23:20.550 --> 00:23:23.355
However, there are also
domestic opportunities

00:23:23.355 --> 00:23:28.288
relating to a rapid implementation
of structural reforms

00:23:28.288 --> 00:23:31.080
in Greece and a reduction,
both direct and indirect,

00:23:31.080 --> 00:23:34.470
of the primary surplus fiscal targets.

00:23:34.470 --> 00:23:37.220
The fact that Greece still lags behind

00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:40.650
it's piercing competitors
in almost all industries

00:23:40.650 --> 00:23:43.252
of structural competitiveness,
is a huge opportunity

00:23:43.252 --> 00:23:47.053
for a rapid catchup,
which should be exploited.

00:23:48.710 --> 00:23:51.260
Despite the progress made so far,

00:23:51.260 --> 00:23:53.930
major sought and medium
to long-term challenges

00:23:53.930 --> 00:23:57.363
and crisis related legacies remain.

00:23:59.090 --> 00:24:02.800
The main medium to long term
challenges are the following:

00:24:02.800 --> 00:24:05.950
the high public debt, who sets
an ability of goals improves

00:24:05.950 --> 00:24:08.990
significantly in the medium
term with a mesas adopted

00:24:08.990 --> 00:24:12.860
by the Eurogroup 2012 to 2018,

00:24:12.860 --> 00:24:15.980
created uncertainty about business ability

00:24:15.980 --> 00:24:18.665
to service it's debt in the long-term.

00:24:18.665 --> 00:24:20.920
In the medium term, there's no problem.

00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:25.460
Over the next 10 years, we have
no debt servicing problems.

00:24:25.460 --> 00:24:27.610
Raising the cost of borrowing
both from the public

00:24:27.610 --> 00:24:30.773
and the private sector and
harboring growth prospects.

00:24:31.830 --> 00:24:33.850
Greece's negative current account balance

00:24:33.850 --> 00:24:37.343
and large negative net
international investment position.

00:24:38.280 --> 00:24:40.340
The high long term unemployment rate,

00:24:40.340 --> 00:24:43.630
which generates inequalities,
threatening social cohesion

00:24:43.630 --> 00:24:46.463
and increases the risk
of human capital erosion.

00:24:47.390 --> 00:24:51.273
The projected demographic
decline due to population aging,

00:24:52.490 --> 00:24:56.170
but also outward migration, which excerpts

00:24:56.170 --> 00:24:59.370
downward precedent potential
growth and puts at risk,

00:24:59.370 --> 00:25:02.380
the long term system ability
of the pension system.

00:25:02.380 --> 00:25:05.240
The slow digital
transformation of the economy,

00:25:05.240 --> 00:25:07.670
based on the digital
economy and society index

00:25:07.670 --> 00:25:12.110
of the European commission,
Greece for the year 2019

00:25:12.110 --> 00:25:16.217
ranks 26th among the 28 EU
countries, which implies

00:25:16.217 --> 00:25:20.293
a high risk of technological
lack and digital illiteracy.

00:25:21.220 --> 00:25:25.507
The multiyear recession
has left an investment gap

00:25:25.507 --> 00:25:29.480
and risks permanently impairing
the productive capacity

00:25:29.480 --> 00:25:32.630
of the Greek economy
through a hysteresis effect.

00:25:32.630 --> 00:25:35.550
In more detail, gross
fixed cut of formation

00:25:35.550 --> 00:25:40.360
of current prices fell
from 26% of GDP in 2007

00:25:40.360 --> 00:25:45.360
that is before the crisis,
to 11.1% of GDP in 2018.

00:25:46.040 --> 00:25:50.580
The largest proportion of
this decline at the standout

00:25:50.580 --> 00:25:53.420
of 15 percentage points,
is due to shrinking

00:25:53.420 --> 00:25:55.740
the residential investment, which fell

00:25:55.740 --> 00:25:59.540
from 10.8% of GDP in 2007
to 0.7% of GDP in 2018.

00:26:03.100 --> 00:26:06.750
Fixed capital investment,
net of depreciation,

00:26:06.750 --> 00:26:09.510
has been negative since 2011.

00:26:09.510 --> 00:26:13.840
Specifically in 2018, net
fixed capital investment

00:26:13.840 --> 00:26:17.290
amounted to roughly minus 8.8 billion

00:26:17.290 --> 00:26:20.763
or minus 4.8% of nominal GDP.

00:26:21.750 --> 00:26:24.120
Positive net investment is a prerequisite.

00:26:24.120 --> 00:26:26.650
If a capital stock
invest a potential output

00:26:26.650 --> 00:26:28.683
of the Greek economy are to increase,

00:26:29.580 --> 00:26:31.580
estimates by the Bank of Greece indicate

00:26:31.580 --> 00:26:33.920
that the net capital
stock of the Greek economy

00:26:33.920 --> 00:26:38.920
at constant 2010 prices
decline by 67.4 billion euros

00:26:39.630 --> 00:26:44.630
in the period 2010-2016 to
622.2 billion euros in 2016.

00:26:47.702 --> 00:26:50.710
In order to raise the net capital stock

00:26:50.710 --> 00:26:53.760
over the next decade to pre-crisis levels,

00:26:53.760 --> 00:26:56.780
growth fixed capital
formation at constant prices

00:26:56.780 --> 00:26:59.023
needs to increase by about 10% a year.

00:27:00.960 --> 00:27:04.190
However, excluding the
residential investment,

00:27:04.190 --> 00:27:07.930
which accounts for about
50% of the capital stock,

00:27:07.930 --> 00:27:10.570
gross fixed capital
formation at constant prices

00:27:10.570 --> 00:27:14.553
needs to increase by
about 5% per year by 2029,

00:27:14.553 --> 00:27:17.770
that is for the next decade.

00:27:17.770 --> 00:27:20.710
Also, a business investment
growth rate of 5%

00:27:20.710 --> 00:27:23.780
per year over the next
decade is rather high.

00:27:23.780 --> 00:27:26.450
It is deemed perceivable
for the Greek Economy Base

00:27:26.450 --> 00:27:30.170
on Historical Experience so
long as suitable investment

00:27:30.170 --> 00:27:32.220
in business mending policies are pursued.

00:27:33.580 --> 00:27:37.640
Investments needed to
accelerate in order to bridge

00:27:37.640 --> 00:27:39.760
the investment gap in a timely manner

00:27:39.760 --> 00:27:42.650
and avoid the so-called hysteresis effect.

00:27:42.650 --> 00:27:45.219
As recently pointed out by
the European Commission,

00:27:45.219 --> 00:27:48.307
Greece needs additional
public and private investment

00:27:48.307 --> 00:27:53.307
in transport, solid waste,
industrial sewage treatment,

00:27:53.420 --> 00:27:55.380
water supply, infrastructure,

00:27:55.380 --> 00:27:58.740
and energy network connectivity,

00:27:58.740 --> 00:28:02.370
mainly between the islands
and mainland Greece,

00:28:02.370 --> 00:28:06.113
in information and
communication technology, ICT,

00:28:07.026 --> 00:28:09.223
and in innovation,
education, and training.

00:28:10.560 --> 00:28:14.150
Many of the above investments would align

00:28:14.150 --> 00:28:16.150
Greece's environmental protection startups

00:28:16.150 --> 00:28:18.720
with those of the rest
of the European Union,

00:28:18.720 --> 00:28:21.640
something particularly important

00:28:21.640 --> 00:28:24.440
given the risks of climatic change.

00:28:24.440 --> 00:28:27.190
Addressing the challenges
of climate change calls

00:28:27.190 --> 00:28:29.130
for coordinated efforts.

00:28:29.130 --> 00:28:32.100
Incidentally, the bank of Greece has been

00:28:32.100 --> 00:28:33.840
playing an active role in this area

00:28:33.840 --> 00:28:36.430
through it's Climate Change
Impact Studies Committee

00:28:36.430 --> 00:28:38.800
and it's various
publications of the topic.

00:28:38.800 --> 00:28:41.530
Moreover, the Bank of Greece participates

00:28:41.530 --> 00:28:43.740
in the Central Banks
and Supervisors Network

00:28:43.740 --> 00:28:45.930
for Greening the Financial System,

00:28:45.930 --> 00:28:49.330
aiming to enhance the role
of the financial system

00:28:49.330 --> 00:28:52.090
in managing climate and
environmental risks,

00:28:52.090 --> 00:28:55.120
analyze the micro financial
impact of climate change,

00:28:55.120 --> 00:28:57.200
and strengthen the global response

00:28:57.200 --> 00:28:58.863
to the threat of climate change.

00:29:01.580 --> 00:29:04.527
Apart from the medium
to long term challenges,

00:29:04.527 --> 00:29:07.270
the Greek economy also
faces major challenges

00:29:07.270 --> 00:29:09.540
in the immediate future,
which need to be dealt

00:29:09.540 --> 00:29:11.133
with as a matter of urgency.

00:29:12.160 --> 00:29:14.030
Greek government bonds have yet

00:29:14.030 --> 00:29:16.580
to regain investment rate stages,

00:29:16.580 --> 00:29:18.300
despite the substantial decline

00:29:18.300 --> 00:29:21.280
in the yields after the
new government took office.

00:29:21.280 --> 00:29:22.800
And the recent successful issuance

00:29:22.800 --> 00:29:24.780
of a new seven-year Greek government bond

00:29:24.780 --> 00:29:28.240
at the yield of 1.9% with
significant participation

00:29:28.240 --> 00:29:29.927
from foreign institutional investors.

00:29:29.927 --> 00:29:34.927
Recently, 10-year government
bond hits fell below 1.4%.

00:29:35.130 --> 00:29:36.950
And what is even more important,

00:29:36.950 --> 00:29:41.163
the corresponding spread
fell below 200 basis points.

00:29:41.163 --> 00:29:44.935
Most fell below 190 basis points today.

00:29:44.935 --> 00:29:47.890
It is estimated that
investment Greek statures

00:29:47.890 --> 00:29:51.363
could cut further the
spread by 60 basis points.

00:29:52.930 --> 00:29:55.220
The Greek economy continues to face

00:29:55.220 --> 00:29:57.810
very tight fiscal and monetary conditions,

00:29:57.810 --> 00:30:01.020
compared to all the other
member states of the Euro area,

00:30:01.020 --> 00:30:03.100
which negatively affect
its growth prospects

00:30:03.100 --> 00:30:04.603
and overall competitiveness.

00:30:05.480 --> 00:30:08.840
Parameter surpluses in recent
years have been very large.

00:30:08.840 --> 00:30:10.640
The high parameter surplus targets

00:30:10.640 --> 00:30:12.520
and their systematic overachievement

00:30:12.520 --> 00:30:14.620
in recent years through the curtailment

00:30:14.620 --> 00:30:17.490
of public investment
spending and high taxes,

00:30:17.490 --> 00:30:20.320
have dampened the growth
dynamics of the economy,

00:30:20.320 --> 00:30:22.410
reduced the competitiveness
of Greek businesses,

00:30:22.410 --> 00:30:24.581
created a disincentive to work and invest,

00:30:24.581 --> 00:30:28.830
and caused tax fatigue,
leading to a contraction

00:30:28.830 --> 00:30:31.139
of the tax base and an exhaustion

00:30:31.139 --> 00:30:32.989
of tax bases and tax paying capacity.

00:30:34.470 --> 00:30:36.860
The monetary policies given by the ACB

00:30:36.860 --> 00:30:40.120
has undoubtedly benefited Greek
businesses and households,

00:30:40.120 --> 00:30:42.618
but not to the extent that it would have

00:30:42.618 --> 00:30:45.945
if Greek government
bonds had been eligible

00:30:45.945 --> 00:30:48.527
for the acid purchase program, the APP.

00:30:49.830 --> 00:30:52.720
It is not eligible because we
don't have still investment

00:30:52.720 --> 00:30:56.450
rates or we don't have a
precautionary credit line.

00:30:56.450 --> 00:31:00.290
The fact that all the
other member states enjoy

00:31:00.290 --> 00:31:02.450
much more favorable financial conditions

00:31:02.450 --> 00:31:05.890
for their businesses has an
undoubtedly negative impact

00:31:07.031 --> 00:31:09.200
on Greece's overall competitiveness.

00:31:09.200 --> 00:31:11.695
The highest stock of non
performing loans impairs

00:31:11.695 --> 00:31:14.926
bank's lending capacity and
increases lending costs.

00:31:14.926 --> 00:31:17.410
This is yet another reason on top

00:31:17.410 --> 00:31:19.960
of the previous one just mentioned,

00:31:19.960 --> 00:31:23.330
why Greek businesses continue
to face higher financing costs

00:31:23.330 --> 00:31:25.100
than their European counterparts

00:31:25.100 --> 00:31:27.610
which undermine their
competitive position.

00:31:27.610 --> 00:31:29.832
Despite the significant
drop in unit labor costs,

00:31:29.832 --> 00:31:31.948
following the wide range of reforms

00:31:31.948 --> 00:31:35.253
that were implemented in recent years.

00:31:35.253 --> 00:31:37.660
It is indicative that according

00:31:37.660 --> 00:31:39.774
to the most recently available data,

00:31:39.774 --> 00:31:42.200
the average bank lending
rate for businesses

00:31:42.200 --> 00:31:45.380
in Greece is still slightly below 5%,

00:31:45.380 --> 00:31:48.163
compared to slightly
above 2% in the Euro area.

00:31:50.170 --> 00:31:52.230
Up to now, the business environment

00:31:52.230 --> 00:31:54.870
had not been considered
investment friendly

00:31:54.870 --> 00:31:58.060
and in fact, discouraged investment.

00:31:58.060 --> 00:31:59.640
Non-price competitiveness,

00:31:59.640 --> 00:32:01.810
so-called structural competitiveness,

00:32:01.810 --> 00:32:05.970
is very low compared to
Greece's EU partners.

00:32:05.970 --> 00:32:08.010
This is mainly due to high tax rates,

00:32:08.010 --> 00:32:09.780
weak public sector efficiency,

00:32:09.780 --> 00:32:12.149
and delays in court
proceedings and rulings.

00:32:12.149 --> 00:32:14.149
Here are some numbers.

00:32:14.149 --> 00:32:18.940
According to the World
Economic Forum in October 2018,

00:32:18.940 --> 00:32:23.940
Greece ranked 103rd out of 140 countries

00:32:26.010 --> 00:32:29.470
in check in balances, which
refers to budget transparency,

00:32:29.470 --> 00:32:32.710
judicial independence,
efficiency of legal framework,

00:32:32.710 --> 00:32:36.370
and challenging regulations
and freedom of the press.

00:32:36.370 --> 00:32:41.200
115th in public sector
performance, which is first.

00:32:41.200 --> 00:32:43.153
To the man, who got in my relations.

00:32:43.153 --> 00:32:46.580
Efficiency of legal framework
in settling disputes,

00:32:46.580 --> 00:32:50.320
in participation index future
orientation of government.

00:32:50.320 --> 00:32:53.110
119th in property rights protection,

00:32:53.110 --> 00:32:55.360
which refers to property rights,

00:32:55.360 --> 00:32:56.940
intellectual property protection

00:32:56.940 --> 00:32:58.560
and quality of legal administration.

00:32:58.560 --> 00:33:02.040
And 119th again, as
regards to the strength

00:33:02.040 --> 00:33:04.433
of auditing and reporting standards.

00:33:05.620 --> 00:33:06.850
According to the world banks

00:33:06.850 --> 00:33:09.890
of doing business reports for 2019,

00:33:09.890 --> 00:33:14.890
Greece ranks 132nd out of 190 countries

00:33:15.530 --> 00:33:18.320
in terms of enforcing contracts.

00:33:18.320 --> 00:33:22.540
Specifically, it takes
1,580 days for a case

00:33:22.540 --> 00:33:25.620
to be heard by the competent
court of first instance

00:33:25.620 --> 00:33:27.750
and for the ruling to be enforced,

00:33:27.750 --> 00:33:32.750
compared to only 582 days in
the EUCD high-income economies.

00:33:34.210 --> 00:33:37.270
And resolving insolvency takes 3.5 years

00:33:37.270 --> 00:33:41.990
compared to 1.7 years in the
EUCD high-income economies.

00:33:41.990 --> 00:33:46.695
Thus, the recovery rate
is 33.2% in Greece.

00:33:46.695 --> 00:33:51.112
It gained 70% in the EUCD
high-income economies.

00:33:52.959 --> 00:33:56.998
The reform's agenda of
the new Greek government

00:33:56.998 --> 00:34:01.440
elected last July is viewed positively

00:34:01.440 --> 00:34:03.580
by the international financial markets,

00:34:03.580 --> 00:34:06.043
as indicated by the rapid decline

00:34:06.043 --> 00:34:10.150
in Greek government bond
yields, which as I already said,

00:34:10.150 --> 00:34:12.163
currently stand at below 1.4%.

00:34:13.260 --> 00:34:15.030
The government is swiftly implementing

00:34:15.030 --> 00:34:17.610
it's planned investment
growth strengthening polices,

00:34:17.610 --> 00:34:20.170
which involve lowering business taxes

00:34:20.170 --> 00:34:23.490
and placing more emphasis on
the reform and privatizations.

00:34:23.490 --> 00:34:26.170
As a means to address short
and long-term challenges

00:34:26.170 --> 00:34:29.110
and to reign force credibility
of economic policy.

00:34:29.110 --> 00:34:31.230
Meanwhile, the substantial improvement

00:34:31.230 --> 00:34:33.040
in positive execution, according

00:34:33.040 --> 00:34:35.700
to recently published
Bank of Greece caste data,

00:34:35.700 --> 00:34:40.010
between June and August 2019, indicate

00:34:40.010 --> 00:34:45.010
that the primary surplus fiscal
target for 2019 will be met.

00:34:45.043 --> 00:34:47.720
This should support the efforts

00:34:47.720 --> 00:34:49.660
of the Greek government
to achieve and upgrade

00:34:49.660 --> 00:34:52.770
of investment bonds, to
investment rate stages

00:34:52.770 --> 00:34:56.160
by international
accrediting organizations.

00:34:56.160 --> 00:34:58.567
Should this happen, Greek bonds

00:34:58.567 --> 00:35:00.640
will then be allowed to participate

00:35:00.640 --> 00:35:04.370
in recently enhanced
acid purchase program.

00:35:04.370 --> 00:35:06.940
And therefore to reach
substantial benefits

00:35:06.940 --> 00:35:10.020
in terms of lower borrowing
costs for the Greek economy.

00:35:10.020 --> 00:35:14.320
If you remember, I said that this will cut

00:35:14.320 --> 00:35:17.523
about 60 basis points for our
borrowing cost of average.

00:35:18.400 --> 00:35:20.793
The recent economic policies should follow

00:35:20.793 --> 00:35:23.970
a three-pronged approach aimed at, first,

00:35:23.970 --> 00:35:26.180
achieving the agreed fiscal targets.

00:35:26.180 --> 00:35:29.420
Second, drastically reducing
non performing loans.

00:35:29.420 --> 00:35:31.370
And third, stepping up the pace

00:35:31.370 --> 00:35:33.762
of structural reform privatizations.

00:35:33.762 --> 00:35:36.350
The fact that the new
government immediately

00:35:36.350 --> 00:35:38.410
announced that it will respect the agreed

00:35:38.410 --> 00:35:41.400
fiscal target is a welcome development.

00:35:41.400 --> 00:35:44.640
At the same time, in line
with what the bank of Greece

00:35:44.640 --> 00:35:46.910
has repeatedly stressed in recent years,

00:35:46.910 --> 00:35:51.700
the government is negotiating
both direct and indirect

00:35:51.700 --> 00:35:56.016
of the primary surplus
target with institutions.

00:35:56.016 --> 00:36:00.580
A lower, more realistic
primary surplus target

00:36:00.580 --> 00:36:05.280
compared to the current one
of 3.5% GDP through 2022.

00:36:07.240 --> 00:36:10.100
If combined with more
reform privatizations,

00:36:10.100 --> 00:36:15.100
would probably imply lower
rather than higher public debt.

00:36:15.550 --> 00:36:19.760
This is so because with a
public debt to GDP ratio

00:36:19.760 --> 00:36:24.760
of 180% of GDP, a one percentage
point higher growth rate,

00:36:26.360 --> 00:36:28.200
which is likely to materialize

00:36:28.200 --> 00:36:29.950
if the lower primary surplus target

00:36:29.950 --> 00:36:33.580
is received through lower
taxes and social contributions,

00:36:33.580 --> 00:36:37.124
combined with more privatization
and structural reforms.

00:36:37.124 --> 00:36:42.100
Or 100 basis points lower borrowing costs

00:36:42.100 --> 00:36:44.770
which is already materialized related

00:36:44.770 --> 00:36:47.478
to the European Commission's
base line scenario.

00:36:47.478 --> 00:36:49.834
For those of you that you don't remember,

00:36:49.834 --> 00:36:52.640
the base line scenario of
the European Commission

00:36:52.640 --> 00:36:57.640
assumes an average 10-year
bond interest rate of 4.9%.

00:36:58.954 --> 00:37:01.520
Right now it is less than 1.4%,

00:37:01.520 --> 00:37:04.130
so that's a very big difference.

00:37:04.130 --> 00:37:09.130
So, this is 1.8 times more effective

00:37:09.385 --> 00:37:12.970
in reducing the debt ratio rather than

00:37:12.970 --> 00:37:15.820
an additional GDP percentage
points over primary surplus.

00:37:16.850 --> 00:37:20.200
The fact that government
borrowing costs today

00:37:20.200 --> 00:37:22.630
are much lower than under
the base line scenario

00:37:22.630 --> 00:37:25.520
of the European Commission's
debts and ability analysis,

00:37:25.520 --> 00:37:28.720
provides leeway for
easing the fiscal targets

00:37:28.720 --> 00:37:31.840
without compromising debt sustainability.

00:37:31.840 --> 00:37:34.580
Moreover, the stability
and growth part allows

00:37:34.580 --> 00:37:37.800
for fiscal flexibility,
so long as additional

00:37:37.800 --> 00:37:40.023
reforms increase potential growth.

00:37:40.890 --> 00:37:44.180
In a nutshell, there appear
to be sufficient grounds

00:37:44.180 --> 00:37:46.880
for lowering the primary
surplus targets and harbor

00:37:46.880 --> 00:37:49.840
on for a compromise solution.

00:37:49.840 --> 00:37:51.940
In such a solution, primary surpluses

00:37:51.940 --> 00:37:55.370
could be lowered in exchange
for an acceleration of reforms.

00:37:55.370 --> 00:37:58.230
The outcome will be a win-win situation,

00:37:58.230 --> 00:38:01.250
both for Greece and for it's EU partners

00:38:01.250 --> 00:38:04.300
given that Greece will
be able to return faster

00:38:04.300 --> 00:38:08.463
to a high growth path that
safeguards fiscal sustainability

00:38:08.463 --> 00:38:10.780
and the repayment of bailout funds.

00:38:10.780 --> 00:38:13.970
Downside risks relating
to external factors also

00:38:13.970 --> 00:38:17.623
justify a reduction of the
primary surplus fiscal target.

00:38:19.590 --> 00:38:22.630
Priority must continue to be given

00:38:22.630 --> 00:38:25.440
to reducing the highest stock
of non performing loans,

00:38:25.440 --> 00:38:28.009
which impairs bank profitability
and lending capacity

00:38:28.009 --> 00:38:32.240
and delays the recovery of
investment and economic activity.

00:38:32.240 --> 00:38:34.940
As I mentioned before, the ratio of NPLs

00:38:34.940 --> 00:38:39.940
to total loans remains very
high, 43.6% in June 2019.

00:38:40.180 --> 00:38:43.370
According to operational targets
for repair and reduction,

00:38:43.370 --> 00:38:47.260
the aim is to bring the
NPL ratio down to 35%

00:38:47.260 --> 00:38:52.260
by end of 2019 and to
below 20% by end 2021.

00:38:52.760 --> 00:38:55.710
Overall, despite the
progress in this regard,

00:38:55.710 --> 00:38:59.080
the pace of NPL reduction
has not been fast enough

00:38:59.080 --> 00:39:01.550
to bring the Greek NPL ratio close

00:39:01.550 --> 00:39:05.873
to the European average
of 3.1% as of March 2019.

00:39:06.970 --> 00:39:09.332
The activation of a
truly systemic solution

00:39:09.332 --> 00:39:12.920
to the end period reduction would resemble

00:39:12.920 --> 00:39:15.900
an acid management
company, would alongside

00:39:15.900 --> 00:39:18.870
the bank's own efforts
be key for cleaning up

00:39:18.870 --> 00:39:21.220
the balance sheets of
banks for bank lending

00:39:21.220 --> 00:39:24.890
to increase and for
investments to recover.

00:39:24.890 --> 00:39:28.370
After all, similar solutions
have been implemented

00:39:28.370 --> 00:39:31.533
in almost all member states
under financial stress.

00:39:33.980 --> 00:39:36.696
Foreign direct investment
is also necessary

00:39:36.696 --> 00:39:39.920
as domestic savings are insufficient

00:39:39.920 --> 00:39:43.770
to match the investment
needed for high growth rates.

00:39:43.770 --> 00:39:46.580
If Greece is to attract
foreign direct investment,

00:39:46.580 --> 00:39:49.610
it must speed up privatizations

00:39:49.610 --> 00:39:52.430
which mobilize additional
private investment,

00:39:52.430 --> 00:39:56.290
promote private public
partnerships in various sectors,

00:39:56.290 --> 00:40:00.800
and focus on removing major
disincentives such as red tape.

00:40:00.800 --> 00:40:02.900
The lack of a clear and stable legislative

00:40:02.900 --> 00:40:07.150
and regulatory framework,
an unpredictable tax system,

00:40:07.150 --> 00:40:09.670
weaknesses in property rights protection,

00:40:09.670 --> 00:40:12.928
limited access to financing
at high borrowing costs,

00:40:12.928 --> 00:40:16.770
and delays in legal dispute resolution.

00:40:16.770 --> 00:40:18.300
The lifting of capital controls

00:40:18.300 --> 00:40:21.055
on September 1st is an important step

00:40:21.055 --> 00:40:23.443
towards attracting
foreign direct investment.

00:40:24.660 --> 00:40:28.710
In addition to helping
reduce the investment gap,

00:40:28.710 --> 00:40:31.720
foreign direct investment
promotes closer trade links

00:40:31.720 --> 00:40:33.200
with countries and companies

00:40:33.200 --> 00:40:35.000
with state-of-the-art technologies

00:40:35.000 --> 00:40:38.930
and facilitates participation
in global value chains.

00:40:38.930 --> 00:40:40.850
This would increase openness and improve

00:40:40.850 --> 00:40:45.643
both the quantity and quality
of Greek exported products.

00:40:48.530 --> 00:40:51.726
Greater emphasis must also be placed

00:40:51.726 --> 00:40:55.520
on improving public sector efficiency

00:40:55.520 --> 00:40:58.163
through the modernization and utilization

00:40:58.163 --> 00:41:03.163
of public administration
and state-owned enterprises

00:41:03.170 --> 00:41:06.820
with a redesigning of
procedures and responsibilities,

00:41:06.820 --> 00:41:09.037
and the valuation and development

00:41:09.037 --> 00:41:12.173
of staff capacities and infrastructures.

00:41:13.240 --> 00:41:17.170
Legal certainty and clarity
and a stable legal framework

00:41:17.170 --> 00:41:20.740
as well as a speedy
and reliable resolution

00:41:20.740 --> 00:41:23.328
of legal disputes would be fundamental

00:41:23.328 --> 00:41:26.040
to strengthening the rule of law,

00:41:26.040 --> 00:41:27.750
improving the investment climate,

00:41:27.750 --> 00:41:30.920
and accelerating economic growth.

00:41:30.920 --> 00:41:33.500
Moreover, international experience assumed

00:41:33.500 --> 00:41:37.280
that robust economic growth
is achieved especially

00:41:37.280 --> 00:41:39.230
by countries with good government

00:41:39.230 --> 00:41:41.693
and strong, independent institutions.

00:41:42.972 --> 00:41:45.530
Finally, it is necessary to strengthen

00:41:45.530 --> 00:41:48.107
the knowledge triangle that is education,

00:41:48.107 --> 00:41:51.700
research, and innovation through policies

00:41:51.700 --> 00:41:55.550
and reforms of promoter
sets, technology diffusion,

00:41:55.550 --> 00:41:58.210
entrepreneurship, and foster closer ties

00:41:58.210 --> 00:42:01.900
We do businesses, research
centers, and universities.

00:42:01.900 --> 00:42:05.490
Strengthening the knowledge
triangle and information

00:42:05.490 --> 00:42:08.750
and communication technologies would lead

00:42:08.750 --> 00:42:11.720
to the digital
transformation of the economy

00:42:11.720 --> 00:42:14.060
and increase in the stock of knowledge

00:42:14.060 --> 00:42:16.410
and productive capital, with development

00:42:16.410 --> 00:42:19.320
of outward-oriented
sectors and more generally,

00:42:19.320 --> 00:42:21.223
to acknowledge economy and society.

00:42:24.070 --> 00:42:28.006
Ladies and gentlemen, Greece
belongs to the Euro area.

00:42:28.006 --> 00:42:29.590
It is directly affected by

00:42:29.590 --> 00:42:31.956
it's economic and financial conditions.

00:42:31.956 --> 00:42:35.260
Hence, Greece has a very strong interest

00:42:35.260 --> 00:42:37.600
in promoting and supporting policies

00:42:37.600 --> 00:42:39.533
that strengthen the Euro area economy.

00:42:40.530 --> 00:42:42.815
Policymakers around the world have learned

00:42:42.815 --> 00:42:44.853
the lessons from the Great Depression.

00:42:45.719 --> 00:42:47.596
A financial system in distress

00:42:47.596 --> 00:42:51.870
requires active central bank intervention.

00:42:51.870 --> 00:42:54.880
Thus, when the need
arose and in the absence

00:42:54.880 --> 00:42:57.945
of an appropriate policy
response by governments,

00:42:57.945 --> 00:43:02.880
the European Center Bank
stepped in decisively

00:43:02.880 --> 00:43:04.730
to restore market confidence,

00:43:04.730 --> 00:43:06.460
contain the sovereign debt crisis,

00:43:06.460 --> 00:43:08.370
and support the Euro area economy

00:43:08.370 --> 00:43:11.551
by safeguarding price
and financial stability.

00:43:11.551 --> 00:43:14.750
The European Center
Bank used the asset side

00:43:14.750 --> 00:43:17.050
of it's balance sheet
as well as other tools

00:43:17.050 --> 00:43:20.460
such as for good guidance,
in addition to it's standard

00:43:20.460 --> 00:43:23.220
and nonstandard industry policies.

00:43:23.220 --> 00:43:25.110
Given the success of these policies,

00:43:25.110 --> 00:43:26.980
some of these instruments
will be paramountly

00:43:26.980 --> 00:43:29.730
included in the new standard framework

00:43:29.730 --> 00:43:33.120
as the effective load
bound will largely continue

00:43:33.120 --> 00:43:35.810
to be a binding constraint
on the interest rate policy

00:43:35.810 --> 00:43:39.150
in a low inflation, low
interest rate environment.

00:43:39.150 --> 00:43:43.170
Indeed, earlier this month,
following subdued inflation,

00:43:43.170 --> 00:43:45.540
a downward revision of inflation forecasts

00:43:45.540 --> 00:43:48.481
and weakening Euro area
growth, the governing council

00:43:48.481 --> 00:43:52.350
of the ACB decide to adopt
an even more accommodated

00:43:52.350 --> 00:43:56.250
monetary policy with an even
lower deposit facility rate,

00:43:56.250 --> 00:44:00.050
a new asset purchase
program, more favorable times

00:44:00.050 --> 00:44:03.889
for TLTRO three and a
new forward guidance.

00:44:03.889 --> 00:44:08.889
Euro area governments took a
number of necessary actions

00:44:09.320 --> 00:44:11.690
to safeguard the stability
of the financial system

00:44:11.690 --> 00:44:16.130
and to strengthen the EMU
after the Greek crisis.

00:44:16.130 --> 00:44:18.070
Policy actions have focused

00:44:18.070 --> 00:44:20.670
on addressing institutional weaknesses,

00:44:20.670 --> 00:44:23.680
structural fragilities,
and excessive risk taking

00:44:23.680 --> 00:44:25.750
that led to the sovereign debt crisis

00:44:25.750 --> 00:44:29.020
and the negative feedback
look between sovereigns

00:44:29.020 --> 00:44:34.020
and banks, which in turn,
undermined Euro area stability.

00:44:34.140 --> 00:44:36.500
Other steps taken involved

00:44:36.500 --> 00:44:38.490
not only more effective regulation,

00:44:38.490 --> 00:44:41.370
but also higher capital
and liquidity buffers

00:44:41.370 --> 00:44:43.708
for banks, early warning systems

00:44:43.708 --> 00:44:45.980
and the development of
market protection tools

00:44:45.980 --> 00:44:48.833
to increase resilience
to potential stocks.

00:44:50.210 --> 00:44:53.360
The reaction of the Greek crisis,

00:44:53.360 --> 00:44:55.760
as well as the crisis
in other member states

00:44:55.760 --> 00:44:58.560
acted as a catalyst for key initiatives

00:44:58.560 --> 00:45:01.140
such as the provision of
intergovernmental loans

00:45:01.140 --> 00:45:03.230
to Greece, the establishment

00:45:03.230 --> 00:45:05.570
of the European Financial
Stability Facility

00:45:05.570 --> 00:45:09.390
and it's successor, the
European Stability Mechanism.

00:45:09.390 --> 00:45:11.220
Other initiatives which stemmed

00:45:11.220 --> 00:45:14.390
mainly from the world
banking crisis included

00:45:14.390 --> 00:45:16.270
the creation of the banking union with

00:45:16.270 --> 00:45:18.350
a single supervisor mechanism,

00:45:18.350 --> 00:45:19.950
a single resolution mechanism,

00:45:19.950 --> 00:45:24.710
and the yet to be created
European deposit insurance keep,

00:45:24.710 --> 00:45:28.360
the introduction of stricter
rules on banking regulation

00:45:28.360 --> 00:45:30.498
and supervision, as well
as the establishment

00:45:30.498 --> 00:45:33.400
of the European Systemic Risk Board.

00:45:33.400 --> 00:45:35.710
Finally, the European Commission proceeded

00:45:35.710 --> 00:45:37.600
with the development of a more

00:45:37.600 --> 00:45:41.010
appropriate market production tools

00:45:41.010 --> 00:45:44.173
which allowed for greater
emphasis on identifying

00:45:44.173 --> 00:45:46.870
and addressing system-wide risks,

00:45:46.870 --> 00:45:49.360
the strengthening of the
stability and growth pact,

00:45:49.360 --> 00:45:52.070
the initiation of the
macroeconomic imbalances procedure,

00:45:52.070 --> 00:45:53.493
and the European semester.

00:45:54.600 --> 00:45:57.110
As a result of the above initiatives,

00:45:57.110 --> 00:46:00.250
all member states that had
received European Union

00:46:00.250 --> 00:46:03.750
and IMF systems are
not back on their feet.

00:46:03.750 --> 00:46:05.810
Macroeconomic imbalances
have been corrected

00:46:05.810 --> 00:46:09.004
to a large extent and
growth has been fostered.

00:46:09.004 --> 00:46:11.890
Economic expansion in the Euro area

00:46:11.890 --> 00:46:16.750
as a whole continues on beat
at a slower pace and EU bonds

00:46:16.750 --> 00:46:19.280
have become more resilient
to financial stocks

00:46:19.280 --> 00:46:21.540
over the past two years as reflected

00:46:21.540 --> 00:46:25.270
in the results of the European
Union-wide stress tests.

00:46:25.270 --> 00:46:27.650
Moreover, for additional member states

00:46:27.650 --> 00:46:30.403
who were admitted to EMU
during the crisis years.

00:46:32.069 --> 00:46:35.670
However, despite the
progress achieved so far,

00:46:35.670 --> 00:46:38.840
the Euro area faces
several challenges ahead.

00:46:38.840 --> 00:46:41.648
The recovery of the Euro area
from the financial crisis lags

00:46:41.648 --> 00:46:45.390
behind the recovery of
it's global competitors.

00:46:45.390 --> 00:46:48.180
This reflects weak
productivity performance

00:46:48.180 --> 00:46:52.800
and the lagging behind innovation
and digital technologies.

00:46:52.800 --> 00:46:56.900
Population aging and climate
change raise serious concerns

00:46:56.900 --> 00:47:01.900
about the long term outlook
for the Euro area economy.

00:47:03.290 --> 00:47:06.020
Post crisis who have seen a halt

00:47:06.020 --> 00:47:07.470
in financial integration which

00:47:07.470 --> 00:47:10.963
weakens private risks
airing in the Euro area.

00:47:11.820 --> 00:47:14.750
According to a recent IMF discussion note

00:47:14.750 --> 00:47:18.970
and in accordance to what
has been said before,

00:47:18.970 --> 00:47:23.560
businesses in Greece pay a
2.5% higher rate of interest

00:47:23.560 --> 00:47:26.540
of the financial debt
than similar businesses

00:47:26.540 --> 00:47:29.360
in the same industry in
France, for instance.

00:47:29.360 --> 00:47:32.620
Moreover, for every one
percentage point drop

00:47:32.620 --> 00:47:35.400
in national GDP growth, consumption drops

00:47:35.400 --> 00:47:38.800
by .75 percentage points on average

00:47:38.800 --> 00:47:42.053
in the Euro area compared to only

00:47:42.053 --> 00:47:46.703
.18 percentage points on
average in the United States.

00:47:47.620 --> 00:47:51.360
Economic convergence in
terms of real GDP per capita

00:47:51.360 --> 00:47:56.240
among the 12 old Euro area
countries has stopped since 2010.

00:47:57.470 --> 00:47:59.690
This continues to hold true

00:47:59.690 --> 00:48:03.283
even if you keep Greece
out because of the crisis.

00:48:04.410 --> 00:48:07.230
Only the new Euro area member states

00:48:07.230 --> 00:48:09.640
have sold substantial convergence.

00:48:09.640 --> 00:48:12.720
Divergence has widened also in terms of

00:48:12.720 --> 00:48:16.243
unemployment rates and
income inequality indicators.

00:48:17.227 --> 00:48:22.227
So, bold steps need to be taken
to strengthen the Euro area.

00:48:22.560 --> 00:48:25.810
In the financial sector, it is a priority

00:48:25.810 --> 00:48:27.250
to complete the banking union

00:48:27.250 --> 00:48:29.853
by creating the European
deposit insurance keep.

00:48:30.760 --> 00:48:34.730
The banking union will help
to create a better integrated,

00:48:34.730 --> 00:48:36.790
more efficient, and well-capitalized

00:48:36.790 --> 00:48:38.640
European banking sector.

00:48:38.640 --> 00:48:41.650
Coupled with the completion
of the capital markets union,

00:48:41.650 --> 00:48:45.730
a single rule book for
banks and capital markets,

00:48:45.730 --> 00:48:48.170
convergence in taxation frameworks

00:48:48.170 --> 00:48:52.030
in capital market supervision,
and in solvency procedures,

00:48:52.030 --> 00:48:54.160
and with European union rules

00:48:54.160 --> 00:48:56.960
allowing pension funds
and insurance companies

00:48:56.960 --> 00:49:00.020
to participate in long-term
market investments,

00:49:00.020 --> 00:49:03.040
it can be expected to
support the single market

00:49:03.040 --> 00:49:04.923
and to fund investment and growth.

00:49:05.830 --> 00:49:07.840
More developed and integrated capital

00:49:07.840 --> 00:49:10.853
and banking markets will
reduce funding costs,

00:49:12.588 --> 00:49:15.040
improve the financing of the real economy

00:49:15.040 --> 00:49:17.252
by diversifying the sources

00:49:17.252 --> 00:49:20.240
of financing and facilitate
private risk sharing

00:49:20.240 --> 00:49:22.420
through the capital and credit sonnets.

00:49:22.420 --> 00:49:25.980
For example, as recently
flagged by the IMF,

00:49:25.980 --> 00:49:28.810
if Greece were to improve
it's insolvency practices

00:49:28.810 --> 00:49:30.550
to basic class standards,

00:49:30.550 --> 00:49:32.700
it could reduce it's business average

00:49:32.700 --> 00:49:36.780
debt funding costs by
about 50 basis points.

00:49:36.780 --> 00:49:39.650
More developed and integrated
capital and buying markets

00:49:39.650 --> 00:49:41.790
will also support the international roll

00:49:41.790 --> 00:49:43.790
of the Euro through the creation

00:49:43.790 --> 00:49:46.650
of more integrated and
liquid capital markets.

00:49:46.650 --> 00:49:48.550
However, we need to make sure

00:49:48.550 --> 00:49:50.780
that the expansion of
the known banking sector

00:49:50.780 --> 00:49:53.483
does not endanger financial stability.

00:49:54.769 --> 00:49:58.480
Increased risk sharing is highly desirable

00:49:58.480 --> 00:50:02.250
but we should not forget that
greater public risk sharing

00:50:02.250 --> 00:50:06.063
is only possible with
less not more sovereignty.

00:50:08.100 --> 00:50:10.865
Risks sharing whether in
the form of a safe asset,

00:50:10.865 --> 00:50:13.810
a central fiscal establilization tool,

00:50:13.810 --> 00:50:16.440
it founded to ensure against unemployment

00:50:16.440 --> 00:50:19.150
or a truly European deposit insurance key

00:50:19.150 --> 00:50:22.600
should proceed simultaneously
with risk reduction

00:50:22.600 --> 00:50:25.813
such as the reduction
of non performing loans

00:50:25.813 --> 00:50:29.480
or national digressions and supervisory

00:50:29.480 --> 00:50:32.333
and resolution rules for banks.

00:50:33.180 --> 00:50:36.400
It is only in this way
that we can transform

00:50:36.400 --> 00:50:39.183
what is in effect today in the Euro area,

00:50:39.183 --> 00:50:41.170
a noncooperative zero-sum game

00:50:41.170 --> 00:50:43.223
into a cooperative win-win game.

00:50:44.540 --> 00:50:47.505
In addition, in a monetary
union such as the Euro area,

00:50:47.505 --> 00:50:51.020
the adjustment of current
accounting balances

00:50:51.020 --> 00:50:53.460
should be as symmetric as possible.

00:50:53.460 --> 00:50:55.495
Not only member states with

00:50:55.495 --> 00:50:57.460
excessive current account
deficits, but also members

00:50:57.460 --> 00:51:00.263
with excessive current account
surpluses should adjust.

00:51:01.127 --> 00:51:05.750
Monetary policy alone cannot
stabilize the economy.

00:51:05.750 --> 00:51:08.140
Fiscal policy should also be active

00:51:08.140 --> 00:51:10.760
in those member states where fiscal space

00:51:10.760 --> 00:51:14.430
exist and public debt remains sustainable.

00:51:14.430 --> 00:51:16.890
In particular, the Euro area urgently

00:51:16.890 --> 00:51:20.020
needs investment in new technologies

00:51:20.020 --> 00:51:22.970
in order to catch up with it's
competitors and investment

00:51:22.970 --> 00:51:27.510
necessary to face the
challenges of climate change.

00:51:27.510 --> 00:51:30.110
Part of this investment will be public

00:51:30.110 --> 00:51:33.180
or in the form of
private-public partnerships.

00:51:33.180 --> 00:51:35.620
Moreover, Euro area member states

00:51:35.620 --> 00:51:38.800
needed to step up structural
reform efforts in the labor

00:51:38.800 --> 00:51:41.300
and product markets to
make them more flexible,

00:51:41.300 --> 00:51:44.320
which is necessary in
a single currency area.

00:51:44.320 --> 00:51:46.440
And boost productivity and to make

00:51:46.440 --> 00:51:48.440
public finances more robust.

00:51:48.440 --> 00:51:52.480
However, in learning from the
Greek crisis, the sequencing

00:51:52.480 --> 00:51:55.120
of domestic tax ware
policies is very important.

00:51:55.120 --> 00:51:58.140
For instance, goods and
services market flexibility

00:51:58.140 --> 00:52:00.860
is best achieved before or simultaneously

00:52:00.860 --> 00:52:03.160
with labor market flexibility.

00:52:03.160 --> 00:52:06.360
Otherwise, large real wage reductions

00:52:06.360 --> 00:52:09.800
might occur which are
unnecessary and undesirable

00:52:09.800 --> 00:52:12.803
both from an economic
and a social perspective.

00:52:14.070 --> 00:52:16.750
In the context of economic
policy coordination

00:52:16.750 --> 00:52:19.730
and with a view to
fostering real convergence,

00:52:19.730 --> 00:52:23.210
improvement should be made
in institutional quality

00:52:23.210 --> 00:52:26.483
and good governance across
Euro area member states.

00:52:27.670 --> 00:52:32.260
So, to conclude, despite
some missteps and delays

00:52:32.260 --> 00:52:34.900
in the implementation
of the required reforms,

00:52:34.900 --> 00:52:37.070
Greece has made notable progress

00:52:37.070 --> 00:52:40.160
since the start of their crisis in 2010.

00:52:40.160 --> 00:52:43.100
The implementation of
economic adjustment programs

00:52:43.100 --> 00:52:46.960
has eliminated several
macroeconomic imbalances.

00:52:46.960 --> 00:52:49.370
The economy is now
recovering and has started

00:52:49.370 --> 00:52:53.380
to imbalance towards the
tradable export-oriented sectors.

00:52:53.380 --> 00:52:55.740
The bank of Greece
expected economic activity

00:52:55.740 --> 00:52:57.970
would remain on a positive
growth rate trajectory,

00:52:57.970 --> 00:53:02.430
expanding by 1.9% in
2019 as I said before.

00:53:02.430 --> 00:53:06.867
That is by 2.3% year on year
in the second semester of 2019.

00:53:06.867 --> 00:53:10.000
And double of 2% in 2020.

00:53:10.000 --> 00:53:13.120
The catching up effect
from a long depression

00:53:13.120 --> 00:53:15.020
is projected to counterbalance

00:53:15.020 --> 00:53:19.150
the negative effect of a
serious global slowdown.

00:53:19.150 --> 00:53:24.110
However, significant challenges
in crisis legacies remain.

00:53:24.110 --> 00:53:26.110
That is a high public debt ratio,

00:53:26.110 --> 00:53:29.890
a high MPL ratio, a high
long term unemployment,

00:53:29.890 --> 00:53:33.800
while the brain drain and
other investments weigh heavily

00:53:33.800 --> 00:53:36.033
on the long-term growth potential.

00:53:37.363 --> 00:53:39.430
In order to contain future risks

00:53:39.430 --> 00:53:42.260
and address the remaining
challenges and crisis legacies,

00:53:42.260 --> 00:53:46.310
the government should
implement it's reform agenda

00:53:46.310 --> 00:53:48.210
as soon as possible.

00:53:48.210 --> 00:53:52.353
Because there are clouds in
the international horizon.

00:53:52.353 --> 00:53:56.330
Moreover, the continuation of reforms

00:53:56.330 --> 00:53:58.110
is an obligation to which Greece

00:53:58.110 --> 00:54:00.900
is bound in the context
of enhanced surveillance

00:54:00.900 --> 00:54:02.570
as it will last a precondition

00:54:02.570 --> 00:54:06.614
for the activation of the medium
term debt relief measures.

00:54:06.614 --> 00:54:09.280
Increased policy credibility

00:54:09.280 --> 00:54:11.410
through the implementation of reform.

00:54:11.410 --> 00:54:14.250
The speeding up
privatizations and unblocking

00:54:14.250 --> 00:54:18.650
already improved investment
plans like the Eleni Kon.

00:54:18.650 --> 00:54:20.300
It will increase market confidence

00:54:20.300 --> 00:54:23.320
in the growth prospects
for the Greek economy.

00:54:23.320 --> 00:54:26.930
In acceleration of non
performing loan reduction

00:54:26.930 --> 00:54:29.690
through the adoption of a
truly systemic solution will

00:54:29.690 --> 00:54:33.020
improve financial conditions
for businesses and housework.

00:54:33.020 --> 00:54:35.080
As well as confidence and it

00:54:35.080 --> 00:54:38.580
will accelerate investment and GDP growth.

00:54:38.580 --> 00:54:40.680
The conditions described of both

00:54:40.680 --> 00:54:43.542
will facilitate Greek government bonds,

00:54:43.542 --> 00:54:45.360
regaining investment grade stables,

00:54:45.360 --> 00:54:49.019
thus paving the way to the
inclusion of bouncing this,

00:54:49.019 --> 00:54:52.000
it means recently enhanced
asset purchase program.

00:54:52.000 --> 00:54:55.009
This in turn, would further
lower borrowing costs

00:54:55.009 --> 00:54:56.930
of the Greek economy,
thereby boosting growth

00:54:56.930 --> 00:54:59.110
and improving debt sustainability.

00:54:59.110 --> 00:55:01.000
So in such a benign scenario,

00:55:01.000 --> 00:55:04.980
growth rate higher than
currently projected, above 3%,

00:55:04.980 --> 00:55:08.170
could be achieved through
increased investment.

00:55:08.170 --> 00:55:11.370
This is possible because
the output gap increase

00:55:11.370 --> 00:55:14.401
will remain negative
for a number of years.

00:55:14.401 --> 00:55:18.660
Last but not least, in order
to enhance real conversions

00:55:18.660 --> 00:55:21.210
and strengthen the
international troll of the Euro,

00:55:21.210 --> 00:55:24.780
we must take steps to deepen
Economic and Monetary Union.

00:55:24.780 --> 00:55:26.780
The only realistic way forward

00:55:26.780 --> 00:55:29.960
is to simultaneously promote risk sharing

00:55:29.960 --> 00:55:31.720
and risk reduction measures,

00:55:31.720 --> 00:55:34.600
to improve policy
coordination and to make sure

00:55:34.600 --> 00:55:38.344
that economical imbalancing
operates symmetrically.

00:55:38.344 --> 00:55:43.344
I am optimistic that this,
despite occasional failures

00:55:43.470 --> 00:55:47.120
and backtracking, having survived an acute

00:55:47.120 --> 00:55:50.720
and long economic crisis
once more in it's history,

00:55:50.720 --> 00:55:54.320
and contrary to almost
all pessimistic forecasts,

00:55:54.320 --> 00:55:56.280
has now a great opportunity

00:55:56.280 --> 00:55:59.070
to close the institutional investment

00:55:59.070 --> 00:56:01.090
and structural competitor's gap

00:56:01.090 --> 00:56:04.123
will be experiencing
competitors and cuts up fast.

00:56:06.542 --> 00:56:09.470
My optimism is not only based
on technocratic arguments

00:56:09.470 --> 00:56:11.800
but also on historical ones.

00:56:11.800 --> 00:56:14.370
Please allow me to conclude my speech

00:56:14.370 --> 00:56:17.040
by quoting the historian Roderick Beaton

00:56:17.040 --> 00:56:20.480
in his great book, "Greece: A
Biography of a Modern Nation".

00:56:20.480 --> 00:56:22.600
This is actually the last
paragraph of the book

00:56:22.600 --> 00:56:24.103
that I'm going to quote.

00:56:25.057 --> 00:56:29.847
"200 years ago, during the 1820s Greeks

00:56:29.847 --> 00:56:33.147
"were the pioneers who
first mapped out the root

00:56:33.147 --> 00:56:36.717
"that would lead from the
old Europe of great empires

00:56:36.717 --> 00:56:40.047
"to the Europe of nation
states that we know today.

00:56:40.047 --> 00:56:43.057
"No one should take it for
granted that Greece and Greeks,

00:56:43.057 --> 00:56:46.517
"in future, will always align
with the values, traditions,

00:56:46.517 --> 00:56:50.557
"and politics that we tend to
lap together and call Western.

00:56:50.557 --> 00:56:53.707
"Geography and, to some
extent, also history

00:56:53.707 --> 00:56:57.117
"may pull the other
way but as they prepare

00:56:57.117 --> 00:57:02.060
"to celebrate the 200th birthday
of the Greek nation state

00:57:02.060 --> 00:57:06.177
"in 2021, Greeks can take
pride in an achievement

00:57:06.177 --> 00:57:10.267
"that by it's very nature
and from very beginning,

00:57:10.267 --> 00:57:12.887
"has been one, not through isolation,

00:57:12.887 --> 00:57:15.517
"but in partnership every difficult

00:57:15.517 --> 00:57:18.387
"step of the way with other Europeans.

00:57:18.387 --> 00:57:21.087
"It could not be otherwise because Greece,

00:57:21.087 --> 00:57:23.667
"however understood or misunderstood,

00:57:23.667 --> 00:57:28.667
"has always been part of the
modern identity of Europe too."

00:57:28.870 --> 00:57:29.922
Thank you.

00:57:29.922 --> 00:57:32.172
(applause)

00:57:40.886 --> 00:57:41.719
- Thank you again.

00:57:41.719 --> 00:57:42.670
That was wonderful.

00:57:42.670 --> 00:57:45.326
It wasn't much mythology in it,

00:57:45.326 --> 00:57:48.580
but it was an intuitive course
and it reflected your career.

00:57:48.580 --> 00:57:51.560
It was about so many
aspects of the economy,

00:57:51.560 --> 00:57:54.390
covering such a wide ground.

00:57:54.390 --> 00:57:56.970
So we have at least 20 minutes.

00:57:56.970 --> 00:57:59.077
We can take a few minutes
and answer some questions

00:57:59.077 --> 00:58:02.460
if anyone would like to ask them.

00:58:03.937 --> 00:58:05.120
Hi, okay, there we go.

00:58:05.120 --> 00:58:05.980
We have one already.

00:58:05.980 --> 00:58:07.360
- [Man] Can you give some specifics

00:58:07.360 --> 00:58:10.523
about what climate
change will do in Greece?

00:58:12.420 --> 00:58:14.761
What affects will it have in Greece?

00:58:14.761 --> 00:58:19.610
- With the reforms that have occurred?

00:58:19.610 --> 00:58:21.920
- [Man] Well, or in the future.

00:58:21.920 --> 00:58:24.553
- Well, really, due to the crisis

00:58:24.553 --> 00:58:27.463
will have made the economy more flexible.

00:58:28.330 --> 00:58:30.150
Labor market flexibility,

00:58:30.150 --> 00:58:32.601
less product market and
services flexibility.

00:58:32.601 --> 00:58:37.013
You will have improved the
workings of the tax system.

00:58:37.013 --> 00:58:39.060
Greeks now pay taxes.

00:58:39.060 --> 00:58:42.246
Although, still tax evasion--

00:58:42.246 --> 00:58:43.847
- [John] He's asking about climate change.

00:58:43.847 --> 00:58:47.490
- Oh, sorry, you said
about climate change only?

00:58:47.490 --> 00:58:50.690
- [Man] Yes, what effects
will climate change have?

00:58:50.690 --> 00:58:52.950
- The effects of the climate change

00:58:52.950 --> 00:58:54.548
which you can see if you visit

00:58:54.548 --> 00:58:57.217
the side of the bank of Greece,

00:58:57.217 --> 00:58:58.867
you will have a very large study.

00:59:00.430 --> 00:59:01.969
Greece being a Mediterranean country

00:59:01.969 --> 00:59:05.420
will face serious problems here

00:59:05.420 --> 00:59:08.480
in the cultural sector
and in the tourist sector.

00:59:08.480 --> 00:59:09.420
That's why...

00:59:10.790 --> 00:59:11.623
Sorry.

00:59:12.540 --> 00:59:17.540
This is why we need to invest
heavily in climatic change.

00:59:18.650 --> 00:59:23.370
But acting alone is not the solution.

00:59:23.370 --> 00:59:27.130
We need a much more coordinated
solution as you know.

00:59:27.130 --> 00:59:32.050
So, certain large countries
staying out doesn't help.

00:59:32.970 --> 00:59:37.737
And if the problem is very
acute and it might already

00:59:39.858 --> 00:59:44.820
have started to create
serious consequences.

00:59:44.820 --> 00:59:48.159
The melting of ice in the Anarctic

00:59:48.159 --> 00:59:50.943
has started already, I'm afraid.

00:59:51.940 --> 00:59:54.253
So, we should have started yesterday.

01:00:00.750 --> 01:00:02.863
- [Audience Member] Thank
you for your remarks.

01:00:03.800 --> 01:00:06.300
You made significant emphasis

01:00:06.300 --> 01:00:09.480
on questioning non performing loans.

01:00:09.480 --> 01:00:13.120
In fact, you mentioned it many times.

01:00:13.120 --> 01:00:18.050
43% of loans outstanding
are not performing,

01:00:18.050 --> 01:00:18.950
is that correct?

01:00:18.950 --> 01:00:19.951
- Yes.

01:00:19.951 --> 01:00:20.784
Unfortunately.

01:00:20.784 --> 01:00:22.420
- [Audience Member]
Isn't that the definition

01:00:22.420 --> 01:00:24.613
of a bank that is dead on arrival?

01:00:27.882 --> 01:00:29.298
It's a zombie.

01:00:29.298 --> 01:00:33.450
In the United States I
think the account was,

01:00:33.450 --> 01:00:36.849
correct me if I'm wrong,
but it was a loan that says,

01:00:36.849 --> 01:00:38.023
"Hey, I shouldn't price this."

01:00:38.023 --> 01:00:41.390
Anyway, savings and loans associations

01:00:41.390 --> 01:00:46.110
had terrific amounts on
non performing loans.

01:00:46.110 --> 01:00:49.270
Those had to be wiped away in order

01:00:49.270 --> 01:00:52.213
for the economy to get over the crisis.

01:00:54.651 --> 01:00:59.651
As the account was despite
of what I'm saying.

01:01:00.420 --> 01:01:02.100
- Yes, it is true.

01:01:02.100 --> 01:01:05.293
This the main legacy of the crisis.

01:01:06.610 --> 01:01:11.610
It doesn't have to do with
problems with the banking system.

01:01:13.010 --> 01:01:15.302
It decreased with the sovereign debt

01:01:15.302 --> 01:01:17.950
that the crisis, which
has impacted on bonds.

01:01:17.950 --> 01:01:20.370
The fact is that, in nominal terms,

01:01:20.370 --> 01:01:24.600
non performing loans has the value,

01:01:24.600 --> 01:01:26.790
the nominal value of non performing loans,

01:01:26.790 --> 01:01:30.060
has fell insignificantly
from more than 100 billion,

01:01:30.060 --> 01:01:33.300
to about 73 billion today.

01:01:33.300 --> 01:01:36.410
But the problem is that
the ratio remains high

01:01:36.410 --> 01:01:40.250
because if you reduce, if
you sell NPLs for instance.

01:01:40.250 --> 01:01:43.520
If you securitize NPLs,
you reduce the numerator

01:01:43.520 --> 01:01:47.730
but you reduce the denominator as well.

01:01:47.730 --> 01:01:50.317
That's why in the bank a visual

01:01:50.317 --> 01:01:53.610
can come out to the conclusion that along

01:01:53.610 --> 01:01:57.980
with he strong efforts by the banks,

01:01:57.980 --> 01:01:59.661
we also need a systemic solution

01:01:59.661 --> 01:02:02.790
in the form of aa asset
management company.

01:02:02.790 --> 01:02:07.410
The bank of Greece has
worked out a solution.

01:02:07.410 --> 01:02:12.020
The government is about
to adopt a solution now,

01:02:12.020 --> 01:02:16.587
which of course is not a
systemic one, but it helps.

01:02:16.587 --> 01:02:21.011
We will hopefully be
approved by the economy

01:02:21.011 --> 01:02:24.590
in the European Commission
in the next few weeks,

01:02:24.590 --> 01:02:27.600
and then it will submit for approval,

01:02:27.600 --> 01:02:28.970
the bank of Greece planning.

01:02:28.970 --> 01:02:32.810
So these are the solutions
to talk about, that need

01:02:32.810 --> 01:02:36.870
to be implemented alongside
the efforts of the banks.

01:02:36.870 --> 01:02:39.370
Because despite these efforts,

01:02:39.370 --> 01:02:42.140
the problem is so large as we described

01:02:42.140 --> 01:02:47.140
that despite reduction in
the next three to four years,

01:02:48.140 --> 01:02:52.660
the distance between
Greece and European peers,

01:02:52.660 --> 01:02:55.250
in terms of erasures,
will remain very high.

01:02:55.250 --> 01:02:59.780
This is why we need a systemic solution.

01:02:59.780 --> 01:03:02.240
Not only the individual efforts of banks.

01:03:02.240 --> 01:03:07.150
After all, many financially
distressed member states

01:03:07.150 --> 01:03:09.070
have made use of this.

01:03:09.070 --> 01:03:13.397
So like Harlem for instance
or Spain or even Cyprus.

01:03:19.372 --> 01:03:23.360
- [Student] I wanna
follow up the question.

01:03:23.360 --> 01:03:26.577
- John can you turn up the microphone?

01:03:26.577 --> 01:03:28.766
- [John] The microphone?

01:03:28.766 --> 01:03:31.380
Because the question
will not be videotaped

01:03:31.380 --> 01:03:33.850
and our speaker may not
actually hear your opinions.

01:03:33.850 --> 01:03:37.829
And so, if you have a
microphone, please use it.

01:03:37.829 --> 01:03:39.210
- We have several microphones I think,

01:03:39.210 --> 01:03:40.630
but anyway, we have one.

01:03:40.630 --> 01:03:44.750
So I think many of you may
have had the same experience

01:03:44.750 --> 01:03:47.860
I did visiting Greece a couple years go.

01:03:47.860 --> 01:03:50.240
If course, as a foreigner it was okay,

01:03:50.240 --> 01:03:53.090
but the local people couldn't
take money out of the banks,

01:03:53.090 --> 01:03:56.640
more than a few Euros a week.

01:03:56.640 --> 01:03:58.740
Because during capital controls

01:03:58.740 --> 01:04:00.720
because everyone who was able

01:04:00.720 --> 01:04:03.857
up until the point had moved
their money outside the banks.

01:04:03.857 --> 01:04:08.857
And not 43% but 50% non performing
loans all over the world,

01:04:10.100 --> 01:04:13.510
people were worrying and even expected

01:04:13.510 --> 01:04:17.120
that the banking system was
going to completely collapse.

01:04:17.120 --> 01:04:20.293
There you were, head
of the bank of Greece,

01:04:21.540 --> 01:04:24.460
head of a system on the verge of collapse.

01:04:24.460 --> 01:04:27.480
And now, it seems much better.

01:04:27.480 --> 01:04:28.350
What did you do?

01:04:28.350 --> 01:04:29.200
What happened?

01:04:29.200 --> 01:04:30.470
How did it get better?

01:04:30.470 --> 01:04:34.610
It seems so bad just two
years ago or three years ago,

01:04:34.610 --> 01:04:37.160
how did you solve the problem?

01:04:37.160 --> 01:04:39.380
How did Greece solve the problem?

01:04:39.380 --> 01:04:41.770
- I think the main, the catalyst

01:04:41.770 --> 01:04:43.957
was the return of confidence.

01:04:43.957 --> 01:04:47.790
So, we stand to the outflow of deposits.

01:04:47.790 --> 01:04:49.070
We recapitalize banks.

01:04:49.070 --> 01:04:50.700
We consolidated the banking system.

01:04:50.700 --> 01:04:53.830
As I said, now we have
only four systemic banks

01:04:53.830 --> 01:04:56.163
and a number of smaller nonsystemic ones.

01:04:56.163 --> 01:05:00.500
We used to have more than
20 before the crisis.

01:05:00.500 --> 01:05:01.700
- [John] Confidence in what?

01:05:01.700 --> 01:05:04.380
You restored confidence in what?

01:05:04.380 --> 01:05:06.711
- Confidence in the financial system

01:05:06.711 --> 01:05:10.440
and the fiscal system both.

01:05:10.440 --> 01:05:11.690
That's extremely important.

01:05:11.690 --> 01:05:12.523
- [John] How?

01:05:12.523 --> 01:05:13.890
What made people think things

01:05:13.890 --> 01:05:15.971
were gonna get better instead of worse?

01:05:15.971 --> 01:05:19.260
What was the magic that you created?

01:05:19.260 --> 01:05:23.620
- The fact that both government

01:05:23.620 --> 01:05:27.320
and oppositions finally
discovered that there

01:05:27.320 --> 01:05:32.240
was no other way out but to
follow the orthodox way of

01:05:32.240 --> 01:05:37.240
reducing fiscal imbalances
and doing structural reforms.

01:05:37.430 --> 01:05:39.820
So when this happened, things

01:05:39.820 --> 01:05:42.303
started working more properly than before.

01:05:44.660 --> 01:05:46.300
- Okay.

01:05:46.300 --> 01:05:47.550
One more question to you.

01:05:51.253 --> 01:05:53.407
- I would like to say that on the NPLs,

01:05:53.407 --> 01:05:55.290
I have a question.

01:05:55.290 --> 01:05:58.680
So when the sound importance of disposing

01:05:58.680 --> 01:06:01.770
this number from loans, my question is,

01:06:01.770 --> 01:06:04.662
when this is done, will this affect

01:06:04.662 --> 01:06:08.167
the balance sheet of the banks?

01:06:08.167 --> 01:06:12.271
The question is, who will take
the loss, the hit, that is?

01:06:12.271 --> 01:06:15.890
Provisions are already taken and--

01:06:15.890 --> 01:06:17.110
- Sorry, I can't, I can't.

01:06:17.110 --> 01:06:18.275
- Provisions for this,

01:06:18.275 --> 01:06:22.530
but that are already
taken is the question.

01:06:22.530 --> 01:06:27.280
Or if not, who would take the
heat after this end result,

01:06:27.280 --> 01:06:30.460
and if this will be reflected
on the balance sheet,

01:06:30.460 --> 01:06:32.100
and if these banks will continue

01:06:32.100 --> 01:06:36.382
to make these capital
adequacy rules, et cetera?

01:06:36.382 --> 01:06:37.604
- Okay.

01:06:37.604 --> 01:06:42.604
Well, provisions are about 50% of the NPLs

01:06:43.790 --> 01:06:47.180
and another 50% is the
value of the collateral.

01:06:47.180 --> 01:06:51.633
So actually, the so-called
Texas ratio is about right.

01:06:53.640 --> 01:06:56.010
So the question is of how do we do it

01:06:56.010 --> 01:06:57.550
to liquidate the collateral

01:06:59.120 --> 01:07:02.763
to help banks solve a problem.

01:07:04.690 --> 01:07:06.600
The capital adequacy ratio is

01:07:06.600 --> 01:07:10.300
about the European Union average,

01:07:10.300 --> 01:07:14.973
so we're not solved in
terms of tier one capital.

01:07:18.100 --> 01:07:23.100
The main problem remains the
high ratio of NPLs so that's--

01:07:23.660 --> 01:07:26.173
- When those are sold, it will be--

01:07:26.173 --> 01:07:28.150
- The problem will be solved.

01:07:28.150 --> 01:07:30.230
- No, when the NPLs are sold.

01:07:30.230 --> 01:07:32.650
When the hedge funds, when
the management company,

01:07:32.650 --> 01:07:35.890
will this affect the balance
sheet of the current banks?

01:07:35.890 --> 01:07:40.110
Or this has already
been taken provision of?

01:07:40.110 --> 01:07:43.580
Or it will be shown badly
on the balance sheet

01:07:43.580 --> 01:07:46.670
and income statements of the banks,

01:07:46.670 --> 01:07:50.355
will their financial
positioned be worsened

01:07:50.355 --> 01:07:52.580
after these NPLs are sold?

01:07:52.580 --> 01:07:54.078
That's the question.

01:07:54.078 --> 01:07:56.200
- The balance sheet will improve a lot

01:07:59.233 --> 01:08:02.160
if you reduce the value of NPLs.

01:08:02.160 --> 01:08:03.410
It will be much better

01:08:03.410 --> 01:08:06.030
according to the balance
sheet of the banks.

01:08:06.030 --> 01:08:09.850
But also, let me take one small example.

01:08:09.850 --> 01:08:14.850
Now banks set aside 2%
every year of the value

01:08:16.740 --> 01:08:20.580
of the loans for provisions
so they reduce profit.

01:08:20.580 --> 01:08:25.270
So profitability is being
affected dramatically

01:08:25.270 --> 01:08:27.826
by these 2% reduction every year.

01:08:27.826 --> 01:08:32.230
This is the cost of credit risk,

01:08:32.230 --> 01:08:34.360
so imagine what will happen

01:08:34.360 --> 01:08:37.780
when these will convert
to the European Union,

01:08:37.780 --> 01:08:39.343
or their talks about 0.2, 0.3%.

01:08:41.920 --> 01:08:45.380
So the profitability of
the banks will increase.

01:08:45.380 --> 01:08:50.380
You can generate capital from
high-profitability and so

01:08:52.990 --> 01:08:57.010
you can stop leveraging and
start letting go of the game.

01:08:58.040 --> 01:09:03.040
Of course, gross lending
has started but net lending

01:09:03.519 --> 01:09:07.593
remains still negative because
of the high impair problem.

01:09:10.397 --> 01:09:12.073
- I just wanna put her
question in a different way.

01:09:14.421 --> 01:09:19.030
Very often in these kinds of crisis,

01:09:19.030 --> 01:09:22.130
the banks can pretend that their loans

01:09:22.130 --> 01:09:24.020
are worth more than they really are,

01:09:24.020 --> 01:09:25.730
and it's only when they're forced

01:09:25.730 --> 01:09:28.755
to actually sell them
as the Greek government,

01:09:28.755 --> 01:09:31.770
you are forcing the banks to sell them.

01:09:31.770 --> 01:09:34.960
So one might have expected
that when they've got sold,

01:09:34.960 --> 01:09:36.930
it would be revealed that they really were

01:09:36.930 --> 01:09:39.860
worth much less than
the banks were saying.

01:09:39.860 --> 01:09:41.960
But it seems not to be the case.

01:09:41.960 --> 01:09:45.010
It seems, not for a many have been sold,

01:09:45.010 --> 01:09:48.000
but they seem to be getting
sold at more or less,

01:09:48.000 --> 01:09:49.900
the level that they were marked at.

01:09:49.900 --> 01:09:50.733
Is that true?

01:09:50.733 --> 01:09:51.566
That's her question.

01:09:51.566 --> 01:09:53.760
Is that true, that they have been sold

01:09:53.760 --> 01:09:57.160
at the level that they were valued?

01:09:57.160 --> 01:09:59.080
- They are sold at market prices.

01:09:59.080 --> 01:10:03.540
Still, market prices are
lower than the initial values.

01:10:03.540 --> 01:10:04.634
- Not the initial values.

01:10:04.634 --> 01:10:05.652
But the--
- Than the actual values.

01:10:05.652 --> 01:10:08.260
But market price has improved now.

01:10:08.260 --> 01:10:10.090
And also, the collateral improves

01:10:10.090 --> 01:10:13.950
because of the higher
value of real estate.

01:10:13.950 --> 01:10:16.280
So this is extremely important.

01:10:16.280 --> 01:10:18.500
So, banks--
- Confidence has been

01:10:18.500 --> 01:10:21.271
restored and the whole
economy is helping everything.

01:10:21.271 --> 01:10:23.510
The collateral prices are going up.

01:10:23.510 --> 01:10:25.430
The NPL values are going up.

01:10:25.430 --> 01:10:27.420
- But that's exactly--
- And that's a miracle

01:10:27.420 --> 01:10:28.830
that happened in the last two years.

01:10:28.830 --> 01:10:33.570
- John, this is exactly why
we try to convince our peers

01:10:34.899 --> 01:10:39.090
and partners that it is
imperative to allow us

01:10:39.090 --> 01:10:44.010
a lower fiscal target in order
to improve the growth rate.

01:10:44.010 --> 01:10:47.140
Because the growth rate
is like a global factor,

01:10:47.140 --> 01:10:51.150
which will improve everything.

01:10:51.150 --> 01:10:52.453
The bank's balance sheet,

01:10:52.453 --> 01:10:55.170
the balance sheet of house,
courts, and companies.

01:10:55.170 --> 01:10:59.013
So this is really the catalytic force.

01:10:59.013 --> 01:11:03.970
- [John] I'm trying to
keep track of the question.

01:11:03.970 --> 01:11:05.201
- [Gregory] Thank you very much.

01:11:05.201 --> 01:11:07.285
You mentioned bank capital,

01:11:07.285 --> 01:11:11.880
but in fact, a lot of bank
capital is funny money capital.

01:11:11.880 --> 01:11:13.890
It's not real capital.

01:11:13.890 --> 01:11:15.840
It's deferred tax credits.

01:11:15.840 --> 01:11:18.980
And so I was wondering
if you could tell us

01:11:18.980 --> 01:11:22.830
what is the expected,
what are the projections

01:11:22.830 --> 01:11:24.710
for the effectively elimination

01:11:24.710 --> 01:11:29.270
of this funding money
capital, and moving to

01:11:29.270 --> 01:11:31.310
targets which are real money capital

01:11:31.310 --> 01:11:35.940
which will provide a true
buffer for future losses?

01:11:35.940 --> 01:11:37.380
Which, by the way, the funny money capital

01:11:37.380 --> 01:11:41.970
makes the urgency of your
proposal even more good.

01:11:43.190 --> 01:11:47.290
And if you don't mind
also, tell us in particular

01:11:47.290 --> 01:11:50.593
if you can, about public power
corporation loans which are,

01:11:50.593 --> 01:11:55.030
if not handled properly, will
revert to non performing.

01:11:55.030 --> 01:11:57.420
For the Greek banks,
the exposure is mostly

01:11:57.420 --> 01:11:59.630
with Greek banks and
European investment banks

01:11:59.630 --> 01:12:02.220
as I understand, we're
guaranteed to the public

01:12:02.220 --> 01:12:04.530
which also may have some effects.

01:12:04.530 --> 01:12:08.840
So, I'd like to know what
steps are being taken

01:12:08.840 --> 01:12:12.933
to ensure that these loans
will not be reclassified?

01:12:14.641 --> 01:12:17.410
- For those of you that
you're not specialists,

01:12:17.410 --> 01:12:20.243
we say analytics, we first capital

01:12:22.060 --> 01:12:24.693
in the form of deferred tax claim,

01:12:25.989 --> 01:12:30.300
which a claim of the
banks towards the state.

01:12:30.300 --> 01:12:33.940
Why this claim has been created?

01:12:33.940 --> 01:12:38.940
Because when the PSI
happened, banks had damages,

01:12:42.410 --> 01:12:46.070
losses, which created tax claims.

01:12:46.070 --> 01:12:49.863
Those future tax claims,

01:12:49.863 --> 01:12:52.833
they are called deferred tax claims.

01:12:55.023 --> 01:12:59.867
So, now, when a bank has
profits, it doesn't pay taxes.

01:13:02.720 --> 01:13:05.930
If a bank has losses, then the state

01:13:05.930 --> 01:13:09.300
will intervene with a capital increase.

01:13:09.300 --> 01:13:13.930
This is very, very, the definition

01:13:13.930 --> 01:13:16.853
of the deferred tax claim.

01:13:19.434 --> 01:13:22.288
For the regulator, the deferred tax claim

01:13:22.288 --> 01:13:24.500
is a perfect form of capital.

01:13:24.500 --> 01:13:28.340
We do not consider it as
a lower quality capital.

01:13:28.340 --> 01:13:30.110
It's a claim on the state

01:13:30.110 --> 01:13:33.742
and the state will honor this claim.

01:13:33.742 --> 01:13:37.343
Of course, we understand that
credit rating organizations,

01:13:39.342 --> 01:13:41.127
they don't like this form of capital

01:13:41.127 --> 01:13:44.220
and this is why the proposal
of the bank of Greece

01:13:44.220 --> 01:13:47.710
tries at one stroke to
solve both problems,

01:13:47.710 --> 01:13:50.813
the impair problem and the DTC problem.

01:13:50.813 --> 01:13:55.800
That's why when I refer
to systemic solution,

01:13:55.800 --> 01:13:59.280
I mostly refer to the
proposal of the bank of Greece

01:13:59.280 --> 01:14:03.310
who solves at least half
of the impair problem

01:14:03.310 --> 01:14:06.770
and at least half of the form of capital

01:14:08.118 --> 01:14:09.610
that you mentioned, the DTC.

01:14:09.610 --> 01:14:14.610
Now, hopefully when the
so-called acid protection scheme

01:14:21.000 --> 01:14:24.023
is being approved by
the European Commission,

01:14:24.023 --> 01:14:26.520
the Greek banks will make use of this

01:14:26.520 --> 01:14:29.550
which is a positive step
in the right direction.

01:14:29.550 --> 01:14:31.460
But it is not enough in my view.

01:14:31.460 --> 01:14:35.012
We need a much more systemic solution

01:14:35.012 --> 01:14:38.253
in the form of the bank
of Grrece proposal.

01:14:40.330 --> 01:14:41.830
Now, the PPC.

01:14:41.830 --> 01:14:45.200
The PPC is a serious problem,
but it has a solution.

01:14:45.200 --> 01:14:48.490
If you think what happened to the PPC

01:14:48.490 --> 01:14:51.150
over the previous years, it was a company

01:14:51.150 --> 01:14:54.551
where it could not raise taxes.

01:14:54.551 --> 01:14:57.154
Sorry, it could not raise tariffs.

01:14:57.154 --> 01:15:01.490
A company that it could not collect debt.

01:15:01.490 --> 01:15:05.700
A company that it could
not privatize it's assets.

01:15:05.700 --> 01:15:10.700
So, the government will make use of

01:15:11.541 --> 01:15:13.491
several of these instruments

01:15:13.491 --> 01:15:18.160
to put the company back
into sustainability.

01:15:18.160 --> 01:15:21.393
So it does need to write off debt.

01:15:22.266 --> 01:15:26.173
It simply needs to do what,

01:15:27.400 --> 01:15:30.569
I would say, a rational government

01:15:30.569 --> 01:15:35.569
should do for a state electricity company.

01:15:36.120 --> 01:15:40.403
But it has been done all over the world.

01:15:43.890 --> 01:15:46.533
- [John] Yes, you with
the glasses and the suit.

01:15:52.070 --> 01:15:53.897
- [Student] So I have
glasses and suit also.

01:15:53.897 --> 01:15:55.604
(laughing)

01:15:55.604 --> 01:15:59.310
- [John] All right, well, you're next.

01:15:59.310 --> 01:16:00.143
- [Male Member] So thank you

01:16:00.143 --> 01:16:02.670
for your remarks, Governor Stournaras.

01:16:04.820 --> 01:16:09.803
During Greece's legislating counterparty,

01:16:11.040 --> 01:16:14.450
is tilting on the verge of a recession by

01:16:17.340 --> 01:16:22.171
market undilated metrics,
at least there were

01:16:22.171 --> 01:16:24.732
on some type of looking forward.

01:16:24.732 --> 01:16:29.732
So, will or how Greece's
economic recovery efforts

01:16:31.330 --> 01:16:35.730
may be impacted by impossible asleep

01:16:35.730 --> 01:16:39.190
in the typical recession in general?

01:16:40.860 --> 01:16:45.860
And secondly, the question, I heard---

01:16:46.450 --> 01:16:47.726
- [John] Let's take the one.

01:16:47.726 --> 01:16:48.717
- Okay.
- Okay.

01:16:48.717 --> 01:16:49.902
(laughing)

01:16:49.902 --> 01:16:53.980
- So, yes, you have the right to generally

01:16:53.980 --> 01:16:56.230
have two quarters of negative growth

01:16:56.230 --> 01:16:59.113
so technically, it's in recession.

01:17:01.260 --> 01:17:06.260
The reasons have to do with
the imminent trade war,

01:17:07.190 --> 01:17:12.180
which has affected German's
exports to China in particular.

01:17:12.180 --> 01:17:15.960
But also, there are some
specific factors related

01:17:17.090 --> 01:17:20.383
to the carrying duster in Germany.

01:17:21.710 --> 01:17:24.223
So it might or might not continue.

01:17:26.470 --> 01:17:28.410
It has an impact on Greek exports.

01:17:28.410 --> 01:17:30.193
So not a serious one.

01:17:32.660 --> 01:17:37.650
The exports growth we
experienced in previous months

01:17:40.297 --> 01:17:45.297
shows that it is resilient
despite the recession in Germany.

01:17:47.760 --> 01:17:50.260
But the solution must come from

01:17:50.260 --> 01:17:52.100
an activation of fiscal police in Germany.

01:17:52.100 --> 01:17:54.410
Germany has a huge fiscal space.

01:17:54.410 --> 01:17:56.780
Germany has a huge current account space.

01:17:56.780 --> 01:18:00.250
It's not reasonable not
to use these spaces.

01:18:00.250 --> 01:18:03.040
It can borrow, the German state

01:18:03.040 --> 01:18:05.310
can borrow at negative interest rates.

01:18:05.310 --> 01:18:10.210
So it can build it's
infrastructure by subsidizing,

01:18:10.210 --> 01:18:15.210
by having a subsidy from the
financial markets, not a cost.

01:18:16.240 --> 01:18:20.980
So this is why we strongly
urge Germany to take action

01:18:20.980 --> 01:18:25.980
and expand it's infrastructural
and public investment.

01:18:27.580 --> 01:18:29.252
- [Male Member] Will they listen?

01:18:29.252 --> 01:18:31.502
(laughing)

01:18:32.430 --> 01:18:37.430
- I think they are listening
and if I'm correct,

01:18:37.693 --> 01:18:42.108
they will start spending
on climatic change.

01:18:42.108 --> 01:18:47.000
I think this will be the first
public investment in Germany.

01:18:47.000 --> 01:18:49.551
- [John] They could invest
in Greek infrastructure.

01:18:49.551 --> 01:18:51.250
(laughing)

01:18:51.250 --> 01:18:53.050
Okay, next question.

01:18:53.050 --> 01:18:57.710
- This is not, Germany
can directly participate

01:19:01.327 --> 01:19:04.382
in Greek investment
projects, for instance,

01:19:04.382 --> 01:19:08.698
in the energy sector or they can do it

01:19:08.698 --> 01:19:10.573
indirectly through the
European investment bank

01:19:13.950 --> 01:19:18.060
by enhancing the capital of
the European investment bank.

01:19:18.060 --> 01:19:22.480
And the European investment
bank can take action

01:19:22.480 --> 01:19:25.230
and invest in Greece or in the
rest of the European south.

01:19:25.230 --> 01:19:27.740
So there are many ways that Germany

01:19:27.740 --> 01:19:32.740
can contribute to the
recovery of the Euro area.

01:19:33.250 --> 01:19:36.060
The important thing is that
Germany, the Netherlands,

01:19:36.060 --> 01:19:39.130
for instance, and one of
two other member states

01:19:39.130 --> 01:19:43.250
of the Euro zone, they have
enough fiscal space that can

01:19:43.250 --> 01:19:48.250
expand and be the locomotive
and stop a deeming recession.

01:19:50.990 --> 01:19:55.990
Or it's a slowdown in the Euro area.

01:19:59.160 --> 01:20:03.060
- [Gregory] Thank you very
much for, Governor Stournaras,

01:20:03.060 --> 01:20:04.760
for a very informative talk.

01:20:04.760 --> 01:20:07.152
- I'm very glad to see you here Greogory.

01:20:07.152 --> 01:20:08.270
- [Gregory] I apologize.

01:20:08.270 --> 01:20:09.103
I was a little late.

01:20:09.103 --> 01:20:11.800
The traffic from New York is unbelievable.

01:20:11.800 --> 01:20:13.603
- [John] Why don't you identify yourself?

01:20:14.557 --> 01:20:18.180
- I'm the proud father
of a Yale student here.

01:20:18.180 --> 01:20:19.893
My name's Gregory Prestagos

01:20:19.893 --> 01:20:24.740
and I know Governor Stournaras
for many, many years.

01:20:24.740 --> 01:20:26.750
So thank you for you informative talk

01:20:26.750 --> 01:20:29.390
and thank you for your leadership during

01:20:29.390 --> 01:20:32.309
these years of crisis because
all of us were outside.

01:20:32.309 --> 01:20:37.309
We know how much wisdom and
guts it takes what you did.

01:20:39.000 --> 01:20:41.450
I think the general sentiment is that,

01:20:41.450 --> 01:20:44.002
the sentiment in Greece has changed,

01:20:44.002 --> 01:20:44.930
it's huge of community.

01:20:44.930 --> 01:20:48.930
We see a lot of things
happening very quickly.

01:20:48.930 --> 01:20:51.710
I will say when I saw the strategical plan

01:20:51.710 --> 01:20:54.335
of the government, I couldn't believe it

01:20:54.335 --> 01:20:57.638
because I'm used to these
things at the corporate level

01:20:57.638 --> 01:20:58.653
and I saw it at the government level,

01:21:00.260 --> 01:21:03.994
but you refer to the clouds,
there are some clouds

01:21:03.994 --> 01:21:06.994
and the question ended about Germany

01:21:08.153 --> 01:21:10.380
and you talked about Brexit

01:21:10.380 --> 01:21:14.402
and there's issues
generally about the slowdown

01:21:14.402 --> 01:21:17.600
and the gap of the European
innovation and economy.

01:21:17.600 --> 01:21:21.067
So what would be some
quick steps to increase

01:21:21.067 --> 01:21:24.360
the resilience of this newly born

01:21:24.360 --> 01:21:27.800
and very domestic prospect
that we've created on base?

01:21:27.800 --> 01:21:30.350
What would you suggest as
some quick steps to take?

01:21:32.240 --> 01:21:35.990
- I think the liberalization
of the legislation

01:21:37.430 --> 01:21:40.973
governing foreign direct
investment is very important.

01:21:42.120 --> 01:21:43.530
Then the liberalization

01:21:46.629 --> 01:21:50.350
of the networks of
domestic markets in Greece

01:21:51.560 --> 01:21:56.560
should continue, but I
think the most important,

01:21:57.230 --> 01:22:00.280
the catalyst will be, for instance,

01:22:00.280 --> 01:22:04.840
large user legislation to attract
foreign direct investment,

01:22:04.840 --> 01:22:08.960
all the impediments to
following direct investment.

01:22:08.960 --> 01:22:13.960
The revival of projects that
had stalled, they're important.

01:22:16.630 --> 01:22:20.807
So, the international community
expects a new government

01:22:20.807 --> 01:22:24.863
to do a number of quick
wins in the beginning.

01:22:27.270 --> 01:22:32.270
But what I said, the three-pronged
strategy, first of all,

01:22:35.780 --> 01:22:39.570
continued to respect fiscal
target, but at the same time,

01:22:39.570 --> 01:22:43.500
negotiating a reduction of
the primary surplus target.

01:22:43.500 --> 01:22:48.370
Second, a systemic solution
for non performing loans.

01:22:48.370 --> 01:22:53.183
And third, of course, what we
said now, structural reform.

01:22:53.183 --> 01:22:55.290
All those...

01:22:55.290 --> 01:22:59.980
I would advise the new development
minister to do one thing,

01:22:59.980 --> 01:23:03.360
to take the doing business
report of the Gold Bank

01:23:04.366 --> 01:23:09.366
and see line by line, why we
were so low in the ranking.

01:23:09.370 --> 01:23:14.370
And just correct all of these
impediments and be sure that

01:23:16.660 --> 01:23:21.520
in a few months, there's
going to be a huge upgrade.

01:23:24.600 --> 01:23:27.267
- [John] By the way, I
know yours was up too.

01:23:27.267 --> 01:23:30.290
But I'm gonna stop for Yannis.

01:23:30.290 --> 01:23:31.320
I know you.

01:23:31.320 --> 01:23:33.570
(laughing)

01:23:35.422 --> 01:23:39.005
- [Older Man] Thank
you very much for the--

01:23:41.513 --> 01:23:43.441
- [John] No, it should be up.

01:23:43.441 --> 01:23:45.691
(laughing)

01:23:47.930 --> 01:23:50.477
- [Older Man] Thank you very
much for an interesting talk.

01:23:50.477 --> 01:23:54.870
And you said that the
end state of net capital

01:23:54.870 --> 01:23:56.903
is about 620 billion.

01:23:58.224 --> 01:23:59.057
- Yes.

01:23:59.057 --> 01:24:01.880
- So this implies a
capital over ratio of four.

01:24:01.880 --> 01:24:04.380
So on the basis of this calculation,

01:24:04.380 --> 01:24:09.380
we need 200 billion euro
investment to recover the loss.

01:24:11.860 --> 01:24:14.340
How is that going to help what we want

01:24:15.229 --> 01:24:17.480
and how will it impact?

01:24:17.480 --> 01:24:20.613
- What I said is that in
order to be realistic,

01:24:21.920 --> 01:24:26.330
we don't need to increase
investment by 10% a year.

01:24:26.330 --> 01:24:28.679
If we give power to
this decile impressment

01:24:28.679 --> 01:24:33.300
and just put emphasis only
on the industrial investment,

01:24:33.300 --> 01:24:36.480
then you would need an
increase of 5% a year.

01:24:36.480 --> 01:24:40.081
That should come mostly through--

01:24:40.081 --> 01:24:41.060
- [Older Man] I just said the GDP.

01:24:41.060 --> 01:24:42.880
- No, no, no 5% a year growth.

01:24:42.880 --> 01:24:47.880
You need 5% growth a year in order

01:24:47.900 --> 01:24:50.491
to restore the business capital.

01:24:50.491 --> 01:24:53.870
We had a precrisis.

01:24:53.870 --> 01:24:56.510
So we said that this is not impossible.

01:24:58.054 --> 01:24:59.290
This is not impossible.

01:24:59.290 --> 01:25:03.574
But of course, you need
both domestic investment

01:25:03.574 --> 01:25:07.780
but mostly we need
foreign direct investment

01:25:07.780 --> 01:25:10.120
for one simple reason.

01:25:10.120 --> 01:25:14.050
Now, we save about 10%
of GDP and investment

01:25:15.830 --> 01:25:18.513
is about 12% of GDP total investment.

01:25:20.290 --> 01:25:23.203
In Greece, to double the investment ratio,

01:25:25.510 --> 01:25:27.840
we cannot do it through boarding

01:25:27.840 --> 01:25:31.060
because the current
account will explode again

01:25:31.060 --> 01:25:32.293
as it did in the past.

01:25:33.306 --> 01:25:35.200
So we need foreign direct investment

01:25:35.200 --> 01:25:38.110
to cover this gap and this is why

01:25:39.600 --> 01:25:41.350
the new government, very correctly,

01:25:42.490 --> 01:25:47.490
has proved the attraction
of private direct investment

01:25:48.800 --> 01:25:52.470
as a number one priority,
but that's the...

01:25:54.020 --> 01:25:55.267
- [John] We have time for just--

01:25:55.267 --> 01:25:57.004
- And for the domestic investment,

01:25:57.004 --> 01:26:01.890
we need to reduce NPLs and reduce

01:26:01.890 --> 01:26:03.670
the financing cost of companies

01:26:03.670 --> 01:26:08.123
in order to make domestic
investment liable again.

01:26:09.470 --> 01:26:11.210
- [John] Okay, we have two more questions.

01:26:11.210 --> 01:26:14.366
Young lady, you're a
little in the view, but--

01:26:14.366 --> 01:26:15.810
- And definitely Coastal's
got to ask for a,

01:26:15.810 --> 01:26:17.020
Coastal or no?

01:26:17.020 --> 01:26:18.085
Yeah.

01:26:18.085 --> 01:26:21.835
(speaks in foreign language)

01:26:25.944 --> 01:26:27.974
- [Woman] You talked about
approaching foreign investment

01:26:27.974 --> 01:26:30.150
but I had a rather specific question.

01:26:30.150 --> 01:26:32.220
In terms of Greeks abroad that want

01:26:32.220 --> 01:26:35.040
to open a bank account in Greece because--

01:26:35.040 --> 01:26:36.180
- Sorry, I can't, can you--

01:26:36.180 --> 01:26:38.010
- [Woman] Greeks abroad who
want to open a bank account

01:26:38.010 --> 01:26:40.010
in Greece because domestic residents,

01:26:40.010 --> 01:26:41.620
all they need is their tax returns

01:26:41.620 --> 01:26:44.180
but there don't seem
to be peer regulations

01:26:44.180 --> 01:26:47.810
for Greek citizens abroad for
what a bank has to ask for.

01:26:47.810 --> 01:26:50.170
So is there a way to amend regulations

01:26:50.170 --> 01:26:54.580
or clarify what a citizen
abroad would need?

01:26:54.580 --> 01:26:56.000
Or would you just need their tax return

01:26:56.000 --> 01:26:57.370
or something like that?

01:26:57.370 --> 01:26:59.622
- If I understood well, you asked about

01:26:59.622 --> 01:27:03.560
how can you open a bank account in Greece.

01:27:03.560 --> 01:27:06.230
- [Woman] There don't seem
to be clear regulations.

01:27:06.230 --> 01:27:08.980
Domestic citizens, there's
a clear set of regulations,

01:27:08.980 --> 01:27:10.830
but for abroad and Greek citizens

01:27:10.830 --> 01:27:13.520
there don't seem to be clear regulations

01:27:13.520 --> 01:27:14.760
and I was wondering is that is

01:27:14.760 --> 01:27:17.640
sort of what make
- Sorry, I cannot hear.

01:27:17.640 --> 01:27:20.770
- [John] From my understanding,
peer regulations--

01:27:20.770 --> 01:27:23.750
- [Woman] So if you're a
domestic Greek citizen,

01:27:23.750 --> 01:27:25.240
there's clear regulations
for what you need

01:27:25.240 --> 01:27:27.867
to go to a bank and do
whatever you need to do.

01:27:27.867 --> 01:27:29.097
- [John] If you got to a bank in Greece?

01:27:29.097 --> 01:27:29.930
- [Woman] In Greece.

01:27:29.930 --> 01:27:30.780
- [John] And so if you're living abroad?

01:27:30.780 --> 01:27:32.680
- [Woman] If you're living
abroad, there don't seem to be

01:27:32.680 --> 01:27:34.910
clear regulations for Greeks abroad.

01:27:34.910 --> 01:27:36.240
- [John] To go to what bank?

01:27:36.240 --> 01:27:38.637
- [Woman] In Greece.
- [John] To go back to Greece?

01:27:38.637 --> 01:27:41.880
- [Woman] Yeah, and open an
account locally or whatever.

01:27:41.880 --> 01:27:43.420
But there aren't clear regulations

01:27:43.420 --> 01:27:45.833
so I'm asking is there
a way to amend that, or?

01:27:47.910 --> 01:27:51.930
- Greece is a member of
the European community

01:27:51.930 --> 01:27:56.900
so it's banks follow the
same rules as those applied

01:27:56.900 --> 01:27:59.653
in the European communities,
so there's a uniform.

01:28:01.590 --> 01:28:05.035
There are uniform rules in the Euro area

01:28:05.035 --> 01:28:10.035
which determines how
you open bank accounts.

01:28:10.132 --> 01:28:12.800
Of course, there is regulations.

01:28:12.800 --> 01:28:17.380
They are under money laundering
regulation which banks

01:28:17.380 --> 01:28:22.070
take some separate caution
when you open a bank account.

01:28:22.070 --> 01:28:23.803
But there is no difference.

01:28:28.130 --> 01:28:32.233
We don't treat differently
citizens from other countries.

01:28:33.770 --> 01:28:36.600
If I understood well your question.

01:28:36.600 --> 01:28:39.249
- [John] Let's move to the last question.

01:28:39.249 --> 01:28:40.180
It's a slightly more technical question.

01:28:40.180 --> 01:28:42.440
We'll move to the last question.

01:28:42.440 --> 01:28:44.642
- Thank you Governor Stournaras.

01:28:44.642 --> 01:28:45.970
You helped us.

01:28:45.970 --> 01:28:47.747
What I'm hearing is that there's

01:28:47.747 --> 01:28:51.010
a need for foreign and domestic.

01:28:51.010 --> 01:28:54.260
I'm hearing there's a
great need for confidence

01:28:54.260 --> 01:28:57.458
in the Greek economy and
the financial structures

01:28:57.458 --> 01:29:01.380
in order to generate
investment for domestic.

01:29:01.380 --> 01:29:05.050
How well has grace made any progress

01:29:05.050 --> 01:29:08.730
on the corruption perception index?

01:29:08.730 --> 01:29:13.730
Last time I saw that, we were
greased with abysmally low

01:29:15.530 --> 01:29:19.390
for a developed country
so that is one query.

01:29:19.390 --> 01:29:22.750
Obviously, I think
addressing that would lead

01:29:22.750 --> 01:29:25.550
to an upsurge in confidence.

01:29:25.550 --> 01:29:27.737
And at this time a lighter note,

01:29:27.737 --> 01:29:32.230
I went and told my friend
John that the pronunciation

01:29:32.230 --> 01:29:35.169
of my grandmother's village is Vabakou.

01:29:35.169 --> 01:29:36.132
(laughing)

01:29:36.132 --> 01:29:37.440
Yes sir.

01:29:37.440 --> 01:29:38.993
Thank you very much.

01:29:43.490 --> 01:29:45.870
- That's why I said that...

01:29:47.840 --> 01:29:49.380
The fact that we are so low

01:29:49.380 --> 01:29:53.090
in all of these industries provides

01:29:53.934 --> 01:29:57.071
an opportunity if the new
government acts quickly

01:29:57.071 --> 01:30:00.380
to correct all these

01:30:02.780 --> 01:30:04.923
let's say structural imbalances.

01:30:07.570 --> 01:30:10.423
We'll see an upgrade very quickly.

01:30:13.020 --> 01:30:15.440
I have quoted certain numbers

01:30:15.440 --> 01:30:18.740
so that Greece is very,
very low in the ranking

01:30:22.373 --> 01:30:23.727
in all these industries

01:30:26.220 --> 01:30:29.080
of structural competitiveness, including

01:30:30.630 --> 01:30:33.780
how quickly the judicial
system solves the difference

01:30:36.075 --> 01:30:38.070
and how digitalized the economy is.

01:30:38.070 --> 01:30:40.330
So we have a long way to go,

01:30:40.330 --> 01:30:43.850
but there's also an opportunity here.

01:30:43.850 --> 01:30:46.530
This is a problem but
also a big opportunity

01:30:46.530 --> 01:30:49.703
because if we are so low in the ranking,

01:30:49.703 --> 01:30:53.830
we can jump very high by
changing this quickly.

01:30:53.830 --> 01:30:56.386
And there is no political cost in this.

01:30:56.386 --> 01:30:59.470
We can implement it
very, very, very quickly.

01:30:59.470 --> 01:31:02.756
So this is why am
optimistic and I say that

01:31:02.756 --> 01:31:06.380
I'm an optimist about the
prospect of the Greek economy

01:31:06.380 --> 01:31:10.013
because if we concentrate
on these other easy wins,

01:31:10.990 --> 01:31:13.633
we can change the framework a lot.

01:31:15.517 --> 01:31:17.533
- [John] And on this
note, thank you very much.

01:31:17.533 --> 01:31:19.783
(applause)

01:31:23.298 --> 01:31:25.881
(bright music)

